PVD("bhutan_ndp_2024-2029",{"docs":["","BHU NDP 2024 29"],"s":{"1":[[1,"13","4","Ten-Year Strategic Framework for the 13th FYP","the 13th FYP (July 2024 to June 2029) has adopted a 10-year strategic framework.",""],[1,"13","4","Four-Cluster FYP Implementation Approach","it has adopted a four-cluster approach as an effective means to implementing the FYP through enhanced coordination and collaboration.",""],[1,"14","1","National Programme Implementation Framework","A total of 8 national programmes will be implemented collaboratively by Central Agencies, Local Governments and partners to deliver 8 outcomes and 40 outputs, towards achieving the strategic objectives across the economic, social, security and governance clusters of the FYP.",""],[1,"14","1","Integrated Agency and Local Government Planning Framework","Agency-specific and local government plans are integrated into the framework to ensure coherence and the mutual reinforcement of goals.",""],[1,"23","2","13th FYP Implementation and Policy Alignment Mechanism","the 13th FYP integrates long-term strategic goals by focusing on economic development, standardising health and education services, developing infrastructure based on spatial planning, and promoting private sector engagement while streamlining government roles.",""],[1,"23","2","Policy Harmonization for Efficient Public Service Delivery","the 13th FYP will address any policies that contradict or are not aligned with each other.",""],[1,"29","2","Interconnected Four-Cluster Implementation Approach","the 13th FYP follows an interconnected four-cluster approach that aligns with the public sector transformation initiative which began in 2022.",""],[1,"29","3","Thirteenth Five-Year Plan National Programmes","eight national programmes will be implemented through the collaborative effort of Central Agencies, local governments (LGs) and relevant partners.",""],[1,"29","3","Continuation of Routine Agency and Local Government Programmes","Routine programmes of individual agencies and local governments will also continue to be implemented over the course of the plan period.",""],[1,"46","2","Strengthening 13th FYP Implementation Means","This translates into enhancing the means of implementing the 13th FYP, which involves leveraging technology, creating an enabling environment (with appropriate policies, systems and adequate resources) and meaningful engagement with a range of non-government entities including the private sector, civil society organisations, media and academia, among others.",""],[1,"121","6","13th FYP Deliverables and Public Services Delivery Programme","Through this programme, the 13th FYP deliverables and other regular public services will be pursued and delivered with renewed urgency and commitment.",""],[1,"123","1","Government Collaboration and G2G Coordination Enhancement","Through G2G engagement, collaboration within government agencies will be enhanced to avoid duplication, minimise expenses and create synergy in discharging mandates.",""],[1,"123","1","Data Exchange Platform Development","Data exchange platforms will be pursued by leveraging technologies while ensuring compliance with the rule of law.",""],[1,"123","2","Policy Harmonisation and Simplification Reform","existing public policies will be revisited, harmonised and simplified as needed",""],[1,"123","2","Whole-of-Government Integrated Planning and Results-Based Monitoring System","Systems will be strengthened by adopting a whole-of-government integrated policies and a results-based development planning, implementation and monitoring approach",""],[1,"143","3","Annual Performance Planning and Target-Setting System","the agencies responsible shall break down the five-year goals into annual deliverables, with measurable performance targets and clear line of sight towards the five-year goals.",""],[1,"143","4","Performance Coaching and Evaluation Mechanism","A robust mechanism for performance coaching and evaluation is critical to support agencies in their efforts to meet their deliverables, especially for priority projects of the FYP.",""],[1,"143","5","Results Framework and Performance Management System","The 13th FYP's Results Framework maps out key performance indicators from national goals to outcomes, agency outputs and local government key result areas - establishing clear accountability for delivery.",""],[1,"144","1","Plan Alignment and Annual Review Mechanism","All agencies must ensure the alignment of all projects funded by donor and the Royal Government of Bhutan with the 13th Plan.",""],[1,"149","1","National Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","The existing M&E system will be strengthened with a national M&E framework encompassing the M&E landscape, institutional structures, reporting procedures, integrated national M&E systems, and M&E capacity requirements.",""],[1,"149","1","13th FYP Overall Monitoring and Evaluation Coordination","The OCASC, in collaboration with all ministries, departments and agencies shall spearhead and carry out the overall M&E of the 13th FYP guided by the national M&E system framework.",""],[1,"149","2","National Monitoring and Evaluation System for the 13th FYP","Monitoring is a systematic process of tracking the progress of national goals, cluster and plan outcomes, agency outputs, projects and activities, and international development goals.",""],[1,"149","18","Annual, Mid-Term, and Final Plan Review Mechanism","Guided by the M&E Framework, the OCASC will conduct annual, mid-term and final reviews based on the Monitoring Accountability Framework described in Table 6.",""],[1,"149","18","Results Matrix-Based Performance Assessment System","The Results Matrix will form the basis for assessing the national goals, cluster and plan outcomes, agency outputs and LGKRAs.",""],[1,"150","1","Project and Activity Implementation Monitoring through Annual Performance Targets and Budgets","Department of Planning, Budget and Performance (DPBP) under the Ministry of Finance shall monitor the implementation of projects and activities through the Annual Performance Targets and budgets in coordination with the OCASC.","Department of Planning, Budget and Performance (DPBP) | Ministry of Finance | OCASC"],[1,"150","3","Evaluation and Realignment for the 13th FYP","Evaluations are necessary to make the government and public service agencies more accountable to their stakeholders, and to ensure that the 13th FYP leads to desired results and outcomes through guided realignment and prioritisation.",""],[1,"150","15","Annual Evaluation Planning and Commissioning Mechanism","The Cabinet, Committee of Four Coordinating Secretaries (C4CS), and heads of agencies and local governments shall identify areas of evaluation, develop annual evaluation plans and commission them accordingly.",""]],"2":[[1,"23","3","Annual Performance Planning and Accountability Framework","Performance management and accountability will be facilitated by aligning resources with plan objectives, and through annual performance planning and target setting that allows mid-course adjustments.",""],[1,"23","3","Performance Coaching Mechanism for Agencies","A performance coaching mechanism will support agencies to achieve their deliverables",""],[1,"23","3","Results Framework with KPI Mapping","a results framework which maps Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) at national tand local levels will ensure accountability",""],[1,"23","4","National Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The successful implementation of the 13th FYP relies on a robust monitoring and evaluation (M&E) system, which will be strengthened with a national M&E framework that oversees progress at various levels from national goals to local government key result areas.",""],[1,"23","5","Monitoring and Review Framework for National Plan Implementation","Based on the Monitoring Accountability Framework, the Office of Cabinet Affairs and Strategic Coordination (OCASC) will conduct annual, mid-term and final reviews to ensure accountability and alignment with national objectives, with progress measures as detailed in the 13th FYP results matrix.","Office of Cabinet Affairs and Strategic Coordination (OCASC)"],[1,"23","5","Project Implementation Monitoring through Annual Plans and Budget","The Department of Planning, Budget and Performance (DPBP), MoF in coordination with OCASC, will monitor implementation of projects through the annual plans and budget.","Department of Planning, Budget and Performance (DPBP), MoF | OCASC"],[1,"23","6","Evaluation Accountability Framework","Evaluations will be based on an Evaluation Accountability Framework, with evaluation plans developed and commissioned by the Committee of Four Coordinating Secretaries (C4CS), heads of agencies and local governments.",""],[1,"31","4","Gross National Happiness Index-Based Planning and Decision Support","GNH assessments have gradually been used towards evidence-based decision-making, with the GNH Index and indicators incorporated into national planning.",""],[1,"122","5","Frontline Public Service Capacity and Equipment Upgrade","the capacities of frontline staff in central and local government agencies will be built and enhanced, and appropriate equipment will be provided",""],[1,"122","5","New Service Delivery Model Development","New models of service delivery will be developed for cost-efficient and improved services",""],[1,"122","5","Public Service Outsourcing Mechanism","This includes outsourcing relevant services to the private sector where possible by the Public Service Delivery Division in coordination with the relevant agencies",""]],"3":[[1,"20","4","Citizen Outreach Through Civil Society and Media Engagement","The oversight capacities of parliamentarians also require enhancement, along with improving outreach to citizens through meaningful engagement with civil society and the media.",""],[1,"23","6","Social Accountability and Citizen Participation Initiative","Social accountability will be actively promoted with greater stakeholder involvement including citizen participation, to enhance transparency and efficiency in project delivery.",""],[1,"121","6","CSO Engagement and Media Accountability Programme","This includes engaging with CSOs for effective and efficient implementation of relevant programmes and activities, and strengthening the role of media for accountability and amplifying the voice of the people.",""],[1,"122","6","Citizen-Friendly Service Orientation and Collaboration Platforms","the adoption of a citizen-friendly and service-oriented mindset will be prioritised, along with engagement in effective collaboration with businesses and citizens.",""],[1,"123","1","Private Sector Participation and Innovation Promotion","Private sector participation, investment, and innovation will be encouraged through G2B interactions.",""],[1,"123","1","Citizen Engagement and Feedback Initiative","G2C initiatives will promote citizen engagement and feedback to ensure that policies and services meet their needs.",""],[1,"123","2","Stakeholder and Local Government Implementation Partnership","The strengths of all relevant stakeholders including local governments and CSOs will be leveraged for better results and efficiency, and local governments in particular will be key agents of implementation",""],[1,"124","5","Enabling Environment for Citizen, CSO, and Media Participation","As a means to ensure greater impact and accountability of the Parliament, the enabling environment will be enhanced for CSOs, media and citizens to participate effectively in Bhutan's transformation processes.",""],[1,"145","2","Private Sector and CSO Service Delivery Enablement","the 13th FYP will see a reduction in the role of the Government, as it instead focuses on setting standards and ensuring an enabling environment for greater participation of the private sector and CSOs towards achievement of the plan objectives",""],[1,"150","16","Social Accountability Promotion","the 13th FYP shall actively promote social accountability.",""],[1,"150","16","Citizen Participation in Community Monitoring and Evaluation","citizen participation will be encouraged in the monitoring and evaluation of development programmes within their communities.",""]],"4":[[1,"20","5","Public Sector Transformation and State Institutional Capacity Enhancement","This objective will be pursued through two outcomes relating to public sector transformation and enhancing the ability of state institutions for efficient and effective governance.",""],[1,"21","3","Transformational Governance Programme","The Transformational Governance Programme and the Digital Transformation Programme will collectively drive the effective implementation of the 13th FYP across all four clusters.",""],[1,"21","4","Agile Public Sector Reform","An agile public sector will be built to enhance public service delivery and ensure robust economic management",""],[1,"21","4","Strengthening State Institutions for Rule of Law and Democracy","State institutions will be strengthened to promote rule of law and democratic processes",""],[1,"21","4","Cross-Cutting Issues Mainstreaming","Cross-cutting issues will be mainstreamed to ensure a holistic and inclusive development approach",""],[1,"37","3","Governance Ecosystem Revitalization","the governance ecosystem will have to be revitalised to ensure effective public service delivery, improve economic management and enable the growth of a vibrant and inclusive economy.",""],[1,"46","1","Governance Ecosystem and Public Sector Institutional Strengthening","Bhutan aims to transform its democratic and public sector institutions to be more trustworthy and effective in driving economic prosperity and improving people's lives.",""],[1,"58","5","Governance Transformation Programme","The Governance Transformation Programme spearheaded by the Governance Cluster will be another key enabler across all programmes.",""],[1,"92","7","Policy Harmonisation and Consolidation Framework","This requires the necessary policy and guidelines to be developed and put in place.",""],[1,"111","3","Public Service Efficiency and Cost Reduction Initiative","One of the key intents of the governance cluster is to reduce operating costs through improved efficiency and effectiveness in the delivery of public services.",""],[1,"116","6","Public Sector Governance Strengthening","The 13th FYP shall ensure that an 'agile, high-performing fit-for purpose public sector' drives and enables effective governance, with greater integrity and accountability",""],[1,"117","4","Civil Service Meritocracy and Institutional Reform","Achieving this will require developing systems and structures that promote civil service meritocracy, accountability, integrity, efficiency and effectiveness.",""],[1,"117","4","Agency Repurposing and Restructuring Programme","Agencies will need to be repurposed and restructured, with the goal of reducing the attrition rate of 16.33 percent by half.",""],[1,"117","4","Civil Service Competency Building and Talent Retention Initiative","Efforts to build competencies and retain talent should ensure that future-ready civil service organisations are led by professional and strategic leaders.",""],[1,"122","3","Public Service Agencification and Organisational Development Reform","Through agencification - the creation of autonomous agencies within the public service - and organisational development, an agile, high-performing fit-for-purpose public service sector will be built as a key driver for and enabler of the effective implementation of the 13th FYP.",""],[1,"122","4","Public Sector Human Resource Management Reform","The human resource (HR) management system and approach to human resources (HR) development will be revamped and strengthened to enhance capacities and maximise the potential of public servants.",""],[1,"143","1","Improved Performance Management and Accountability Measures","This includes the application of key strategies that make up the salient features of the 13th FYP, and the adoption of improved performance management and accountability measures.",""]],"5":[[1,"22","3","Local Government Resource Allocation Framework","A total of BTN 72,000 million has been allocated to local governments in the 13th FYP, based on a revised Resource Allocation Framework (RAF) that ensures fairness, transparency, and effectiveness in resource distribution to address local development needs.",""],[1,"22","3","Local Government Implementation of Plans and National Programmes","Local governments are responsible for implementing both their own plans and national programmes, in collaboration with central agencies as key implementers.",""],[1,"134","14","Fair Resource Allocation Framework for Local Governments","Provide a structured framework for distributing resources to local governments in a fair manner to address development needs and local priorities.",""],[1,"134","15","Local Government Priority-Setting and Resource Allocation Support","Facilitate local governments to prioritise and address key development challenges and maximise the impact of allocated resources.",""],[1,"135","3","Local Government Annual Grants Investment in LGKRAS Delivery","The LGs shall, guided by the annual grants guideline, invest the annual grants in delivering the LGKRAS",""]],"6":[[1,"20","4","Strengthening Legal Aid Services","Legal aid services have not been fully implemented and restorative justice measures particularly for children require strengthening.",""],[1,"20","4","Restorative Justice Measures for Children","Legal aid services have not been fully implemented and restorative justice measures particularly for children require strengthening.",""],[1,"20","4","Parliamentary Oversight Capacity Enhancement","The oversight capacities of parliamentarians also require enhancement, along with improving outreach to citizens through meaningful engagement with civil society and the media.",""],[1,"21","2","Citizen-Centric Justice Sector Strengthening","The two key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 1) An effective and citizen-centric justice sector",""],[1,"21","2","Parliamentary and Oversight Capacity Enhancement","and 2) the enhanced ability of parliamentarians and oversight bodies to effectively discharge their functions.",""],[1,"120","2","Parliamentary Capacity Strengthening for Policy and Plan Monitoring","there is a need to strengthen institutional capacities in several key areas, including the monitoring of implementation of plans and policies, particularly at the local levels with direct benefits accruing to local communities.",""],[1,"120","5","State Institution Capacity Building for Rule of Law and Justice Delivery","The 13th FYP shall ensure that Bhutan's state institutions are appropriately capacitated to uphold the rule of law - so that the Bhutanese enjoy equitable access to an inclusive and effective justice system and are empowered to participate more effectively in the national agenda and public space.",""],[1,"123","3","Legal Harmonisation and Parliamentary Oversight Reform","the Parliament in coordination with the OAG and other regulatory institutions will amend and harmonise inconsistent acts.",""],[1,"123","3","Public Hearing Institutionalisation for Legislative Oversight","Public hearing on laws and policies will be institutionalised to enable effective oversight and scrutiny of parliamentary and governmental processes.",""],[1,"123","3","Post-Legislative Scrutiny Institutionalisation","Post-legislative scrutiny will also be institutionalised to ensure that laws benefit citizens as intended.",""],[1,"123","4","Integrated Justice Sector Data Management System","The efficiency and effectiveness of justice sector services will be strengthened by instituting an integrated justice sector data management system.",""],[1,"123","5","Judicial Procedural Reform and Case Simplification","The Royal Judicial Service Council will initiate procedural reforms to simplify case proceedings.",""],[1,"123","5","Judgment Enforcement Mechanism","A robust mechanism for effective enforcement of judgments will be initiated, with clear delineation of responsibilities and authority.",""],[1,"123","5","Review of Redressal Body Requirements","A review of the requirements of redressal bodies will also be carried out by the OAG, Bhutan National Legal Institute (BNLI), Judiciary, ACC, NAB and NCB.","OAG | Bhutan National Legal Institute (BNLI) | Judiciary | ACC | NAB | NCB"],[1,"124","1","Legal Aid Centre Capacity Strengthening","the capacity of the Legal Aid Centre will be strengthened forthe provision of legal aid services to indigent persons",""],[1,"124","1","Restorative Justice for First-Time Offenders","The Judiciary will encourage restorative justice in cases involving first-time offenders as part of an overall crime reduction strategy and re-integration and decriminalisation measures",""],[1,"124","4","Parliament-Oversight Body Coordination Platform","parliamentary collaboration with oversight bodies will be strengthened.",""],[1,"124","4","Parliament Oversight Electronic Dashboard","an electronic dashboard with all the critical information pertaining to budget, plans and activities of the Dzongkhags and ministries will be created.",""]],"7":[[1,"120","5","Oversight and Anti-Corruption Strengthening","With effective delivery of oversight roles by duty bearers, Bhutanese society will see reduced corruption and improved integrity.",""],[1,"121","2","Legal Harmonisation and Audit Issue Resolution Reform","This requires all inconsistent and conflicting laws to be harmonised beginning in 2024.",""],[1,"121","2","Audit Issue Resolution Improvement Target","It also requires a larger proportion of audit issues to be resolved within one year from the date of issue of report - to be increased from 40 percent to 60 percent.",""],[1,"121","3","Corruption Risk Mitigation in Major Sectors","Corruption risks should be mitigated particularly in major sectors such as forestry, agriculture and livestock, healthcare, election, public procurement, financial services, export and import, hydropower, tourism and, environment, among others.",""],[1,"121","3","Anti-Corruption Commission Performance Improvement","Concurrently, there should be improvement in the Anti-Corruption Commission's performance score - from 'medium' to 'high' on all indicators - along with increased proactive research and intelligence-based investigation.",""],[1,"124","2","Whole-of-Systems Anti-Corruption Prevention Approach","A whole-of-systems approach will be adopted to prevent corruption.",""],[1,"124","2","Technology-Driven Corruption Prevention Measures","The Anti- Corruption Commission will lead innovative research and technology-driven corruption prevention measures in key public and private sectors.","Anti- Corruption Commission"],[1,"124","2","Mainstreaming of Anti-Corruption and Integrity Measures","the mainstreaming and institutionalisation of anti-corruption and integrity measures in all agencies including local governments will continue.",""],[1,"124","2","Integrity Vetting and Evidence-Based Investigations","In addition, integrity vetting and evidence-based investigations will be institutionalised.",""],[1,"124","2","Proactive Intelligence and Research-Based Investigations","the 13th FYP will see a shift towards proactive intelligence and research-based investigations.",""],[1,"124","3","Strengthened Performance, ICT, and Risk-Based Audit Programme","To enhance public sector performance and accountability, the Royal Audit Authority will strengthen performance audits on emerging or topical issues.",""]],"8":[[1,"117","5","Multi-Year Rolling Planning and Budgeting Approach","A fully operational multi-year rolling planning and budgeting approach should be implemented starting July 2024.",""],[1,"117","5","Monitoring, Evaluation, and Audit Strengthening System","This should be accompanied by an effective monitoring and evaluation system and increased audit coverage of 90 percent.",""],[1,"117","5","Procurement Process Simplification Reform","By 2024, procurement processes should be simplified to mitigate supply risks, prevent unauthorised spending, and align procurement workflows with business objectives and strategies.",""],[1,"122","4","Strategic Resource Management and Fiscal Discipline Measures","Strategic resource management practices will be adopted to ensure efficient allocation, utilisation and impact of resources.",""],[1,"125","5","Medium-Term Budget Framework and Debt Strategy","To strengthen public finance management, a medium-term budget framework and a debt strategy will be developed and implemented.",""],[1,"125","5","Treasury Single Account, Unified Chart of Accounts, and Public Investment Management System","Initiatives such as treasury single account (TSA), unified chart of accounts, and Public Investment Management System (PIMS) will be implemented.",""],[1,"125","5","Public-Private Partnership Promotion and Taxpayer Service Outsourcing","Measures to drive PPPs, and the outsourcing of taxpayer services such as accountancy and debt collection will be considered.",""],[1,"125","5","Public Procurement Improvement and Non-Core Service Outsourcing","Similarly, initiatives to improve public procurement, and the outsourcing of non-core services under the Department of Public Property to the private sector will be explored.",""],[1,"125","5","State-Owned Enterprise Reform and Privatization Exploration","In addition, reforms in SOEs will be initiated to explore the possibilities of privatisation.",""],[1,"134","13","Capital Resource Allocation Reform","Allocate capital resources, including annual grants, based on the principles of objectivity, transparency, equity, and predictability.",""],[1,"143","2","Resource Allocation for the 13th FYP","The first step involves allocating the available resources, both internal and external, to the goals and aspirations of the 13th FYP.",""],[1,"145","1","Multi-Year Rolling Planning and Budgeting System","the MYRP approach will be implemented in the 13th FYP",""]],"9":[[1,"112","4","Policy Review and Consolidation","Existing policies must be reviewed and consolidated, particularly considering Bhutan's current context of public sector transformation and organisational changes, demographic shifts, evolving development priorities, and technological advancements.",""],[1,"117","3","Adaptive Public Policy Review and Refinement","Public policies must be designed to be more adaptive, responsive to changing needs and focused on delivering tangible results.",""],[1,"145","4","Policy Review and Amendment to Remove Regulatory Barriers","all policies that are contradictory in nature and pose barriers to the plan objectives will be superseded by the FYP through timely review and amendment by the Government.",""]],"10":[[1,"14","4","Strategic Sector GDP Contribution Enhancement","the four key deliverables or outputs of the economic cluster are: 4) Increased sustainable contributions of strategic sectors to GDP",""],[1,"15","2","Diversification of Growth Drivers Across Key Sectors","Investments in traditional growth drivers will also be made as well as exploring new sources of growth across sectors including agriculture, tourism, hydropower, renewable energy, manufacturing and the digital economy.",""],[1,"56","10","Dry Ports, Industrial Estates, and Export Processing Zones Development","It also requires development and operationalisation of infrastructure such as dry ports, industrial estates and export processing zones to enhance productivity for economic development.",""],[1,"60","1","Industrial Park and Dry Port Development for Manufacturing Promotion","Manufacturing industries including cottage and small industries will be promoted with the development of dry ports and industrial parks.",""],[1,"61","2","Industrial Park Development Acceleration","The ongoing development of industrial parks at Samtse, Thimphu, Samdrup Jongkhar and Phuentsholing will be expedited.",""],[1,"65","1","Manufacturing Input, Skills, and Investment Support Measures","This will require ensuring the supply of necessary inputs by making the required raw material accessible and available, and by undertaking measures to ensure availability of skills and expertise.",""],[1,"65","1","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction for Manufacturing","Production will be enhanced by attracting foreign direct investment, revamping and upscaling the Start-Up Centre, and through PPPs.",""],[1,"65","1","Start-Up Centre Revamping and Upgrading","Production will be enhanced by attracting foreign direct investment, revamping and upscaling the Start-Up Centre, and through PPPs.",""],[1,"65","1","Public-Private Partnerships for Manufacturing Expansion","Production will be enhanced by attracting foreign direct investment, revamping and upscaling the Start-Up Centre, and through PPPs.",""],[1,"65","2","Market Linkage and Logistics Expansion","Market expansion will be undertaken through improved market linkages and establishment, and improved logistics infrastructure including the exploration and development of new modes of transportation.",""],[1,"65","2","Startup and Business Financing Support","Financing support will include grants and/or low-cost credit for start-ups, new product development, and upscaling; and tapping into capital markets for financing.",""]],"11":[[1,"153","7","Creative Industries Promotion Investment","Investments shall be made in the promotion of creative arts, film, music and digital animation.",""],[1,"153","8","Cottage and Small Industries and Startup Support Programme","Support shall be provided to start new businesses and expand and upscale existing CSIS.",""],[1,"157","8","Business Establishment Process Acceleration and FDI Attraction","Economic Development Board mandated to expedite business estrablishment processes and attracting Foreign Direct Investments (FDI)",""]],"12":[[1,"15","2","Strategic Infrastructure Investment Programme","Investments in strategic infrastructure will be made such as in roads, bridges, airports and railways to boost economic development and productivity through enhanced connectivity, reduced transportation costs, and by improving the liveability of urban settlements.",""],[1,"61","2","Southern Belt Transport and Connectivity Infrastructure Investment","investments will be made in the consolidation and improvement of roads, bridges, airports and railway links along the southern belt - primarily to enhance connectivity, logistics and trade.",""],[1,"61","2","Dry Port Establishment and Operationalisation","The government will also establish and operationalise dry ports at Pasakha, Gelephu and Nganglam.",""]],"13":[[1,"65","3","Construction Sector Modernisation and Professionalisation","the construction sector will be modernised to improve its overall efficiency and attractiveness as a viable employment sector for the national workforce.",""],[1,"65","4","FDI Engagements for Construction Sector Efficiency","The efficiency of the sector will be enhanced through FDI engagements including joint ventures and PPPs, the adoption of new and green technology, and policy reforms pertaining to standards and practices.",""],[1,"65","4","Construction Firm Export Market Linkage Support","To support Bhutanese construction firms in gaining work abroad, market linkages will be strengthened and established.",""],[1,"65","4","Concessional Credit for Green Construction Technology","Financing support will be geared towards incentivising new, efficient and green technology, and will include concessional credit for the use of new technology in construction.",""]],"14":[[1,"61","5","Large-Scale Commercial Farming Expansion","This will be pursued through the establishment and expansion of large-scale commercial farming, in collaboration with SOEs including the Bhutan Livestock Development Corporation (BLDC), the Farm Machinery Corporation Limited (FMCL) and the Food Corporation of Bhutan Limited (FCBL), and youth and private sector partnerships.",""],[1,"62","1","Priority Crops and Livestock Value Chain Intensification","The production, aggregation, processing and marketing of six priority crops and three livestock products will be intensified to maximise returns and economies of scale.",""],[1,"62","1","Agricultural Price Guarantee and Market Access Support","This will be facilitated through a price guarantee mechanism, access to finance for production and aggregation, and by ensuring market access.",""],[1,"62","1","Subsistence Farmer Support Programme","Complementing this initiative, assistance will continue to be provided to farmers engaging in subsistence farming.",""],[1,"62","1","Agricultural Irrigation and Water Supply Investment","Investment will also be made towards improving irrigation and water supply to improve farm productivity.",""],[1,"62","2","Agri-business Policy Reform Package","Comprehensive policy reforms will be undertaken to improve the agri-business ecosystem - including through price guarantee and insurance schemes, exploring the possibilities of engaging foreign workers to address high labour costs and labour shortages, and enhancing agricultural land utilisation, among others.",""],[1,"62","3","Local Procurement of Bhutanese Agricultural Products","Government institutions such as schools, hospitals, armed forces, and monastic institutions will be mandated to procure locally produced agricultural products.",""],[1,"62","3","Research and Development on Native Animal and Plant Genetics","Research and development (R&D) on native animals and plant genetics will continue, for product diversification and the development of value-added premium products.",""],[1,"153","5","Priority Crops and Livestock Production Investment Programme","Investments shall be made in enhancing production of priority crops and livestock, development of aggregators for livestock and agriculture products, and upscaling of existing agricultural farms as well as the development of new ones.",""],[1,"153","5","Agricultural and Livestock Aggregator Development","development of aggregators for livestock and agriculture products",""],[1,"153","5","Agricultural Farm Expansion and New Farm Development","upscaling of existing agricultural farms as well as the development of new ones.",""]],"15":[[1,"69","6","Protected and Conservation Area Management Enhancement","Sustainable forest resources management includes the enhancement of protected and conservation area management, monitoring and evaluation for long-term sustainability of natural resources, and research and development to facilitate optimal benefits from forestry.",""],[1,"69","6","Forest Resources Monitoring and Evaluation System","Sustainable forest resources management includes the enhancement of protected and conservation area management, monitoring and evaluation for long-term sustainability of natural resources, and research and development to facilitate optimal benefits from forestry.",""],[1,"69","6","Forestry Research and Development Initiative","Sustainable forest resources management includes the enhancement of protected and conservation area management, monitoring and evaluation for long-term sustainability of natural resources, and research and development to facilitate optimal benefits from forestry.",""],[1,"69","6","Expansion of Sustainable Forest Management Programmes","forest areas under Sustainable Forest Management Programmes will be increased, and commercial plantations will be created and maintained.",""],[1,"69","6","Commercial Plantation Development and Maintenance","forest areas under Sustainable Forest Management Programmes will be increased, and commercial plantations will be created and maintained.",""],[1,"70","1","Community-Based Enterprises for Wood, Non-Wood and Ecotourism Products","Community-based enterprises for wood, non-wood and ecotourism products will be established, along with a Wood Innovation and Technology Hub to promote proper utilisation of available timber resources.",""],[1,"70","1","Wood Innovation and Technology Hub","Community-based enterprises for wood, non-wood and ecotourism products will be established, along with a Wood Innovation and Technology Hub to promote proper utilisation of available timber resources.",""],[1,"71","2","Eco-tourism and Nature Recreation Product Development","It also includes the introduction of innovative eco-tourism and nature recreation products, and service charges in protected areas for the use of recreational facilities.",""],[1,"71","3","Ecotourism and Nature-Based Enterprise Outsourcing","The development and management of ecotourism products and sites and nature- based enterprises will be outsourced to local communities or the private sector.",""],[1,"71","3","Integrated Wood-Based Industry Upgrading","Stand-alone sawmills will be upgraded to integrated wood-based industries, and investments in ecotourism products and infrastructure will be promoted through leasing land in protected areas beyond bona fide residents.",""],[1,"71","3","Protected Area Conservation and Habitat Management","The conservation of protected areas will be enhanced with habitat management, and environmental code of practices will be developed to promote clean technologies.",""]],"16":[[1,"71","4","National Hydrological and Meteorological Services Enhancement","The national hydrological and meteorological services will be enhanced to ensure timely provision of critical information and services that support ecologically balanced sustainable development, as well as for protecting lives and property.",""],[1,"71","4","National Weather and Flood Warning Centre Construction","A 24/7 National Weather and Flood Warning Centre (NWFWC) and Scientific and Communication Facilities will be constructed.",""],[1,"71","5","National Hydromet and Early Warning Services Strengthening Programme","Key systems and services will be strengthened, which include the National Hydromet Observation Network and Infrastructure, aviation meteorological services, weather and climate services, and hydrological and Glacial Lake Outburst Flood (GLOF) early warning services.",""],[1,"71","5","Cryosphere Monitoring and Research Strengthening","Cryosphere monitoring and research will also be strengthened along with technical standards and research capacity.",""],[1,"71","5","Climate Services Awareness for Farmers and the Public","The public and particularly farmers will be made aware of climate services including weather forecasts, to help avoid losses related to crop production and harvesting.",""]],"17":[[1,"134","3","Safe Drinking Water Supply Expansion","Ensure safe drinking water supply to all households",""],[1,"134","7","24/7 Safe Drinking Water Supply for Dzongkhag Throms","Esure safe 24/7 drinking water supply to all households in the Dzongkhag Throms",""],[1,"134","11","24/7 Safe Drinking Water Supply Expansion","Esure safe 24/7 drinking water supply to all households",""]],"18":[[1,"19","4","Sociocultural Resilience and Community Vitality Programme","The Sociocultural Resilience and Community Vitality Programme aims to strengthen Bhutan's stability, progress and well-being by promoting its unique identity and culture, ensuring the safety and well-being of its citizens both at home and abroad, and fostering international cooperation and engagement.",""],[1,"19","6","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Youth Engagement Initiative","Bhutanese values and cultural heritage will be nurtured and promoted through preservation efforts and engagement of younger generations.",""],[1,"19","6","Diaspora Cultural and Economic Engagement Initiative","Bhutanese abroad will be engaged in cultural events and economic activities initiated by embassies, missions and consulates as a means to enhance a sense of belonging and identity.",""],[1,"45","4","Friendly International Relations and Cooperative Diplomacy","This requires simultaneous attention to conventional as well as 21st century security concerns - which includes the maintenance of friendly and cooperative relations with all countries,",""],[1,"102","6","Cultural Heritage Promotion and Upkeep Programme","the 13th FYP will continue to prioritise the promotion and upkeep of Bhutan's cultural heritage by strengthening the Bhutanese value system and identity, and enhancing a sense of belonging and nationhood among all Bhutanese.",""],[1,"103","2","Bhutanese Youth and Diaspora Engagement for Cultural Promotion","This involves the engagement of Bhutanese youth, and those abroad in particular, in promoting Bhutanese identity, values and culture.",""],[1,"103","2","Digital Dzongkha and Culture Promotion Tools","It also involves the use of digital tools to provide relevant materials on Dzongkha and culture, and to promote Dzongkha usage and competency.",""],[1,"103","3","Cultural Sector Employment and Market Development Initiative","This includes the engagement of the private sector and creation of employment opportunities in the cultural field - including through nurturing traditional and indigenous knowledge and skills among Bhutanese people, the creation of new culture-based products, the conversion of heritage sites into centres of economic activity and promoting the domestic market for local culture-based products.",""],[1,"103","4","Intangible Cultural Heritage Protection and Management System","It also requires proper identification, registration and verification and authentication of heritage sites and cultural assets, as well as implementing mechanisms and systems that ensure their proper management and access to the public.",""],[1,"103","5","Socio-cultural Resilience and Community Vitality Programme","The security cluster outputs across the two outcome areas will be delivered through the implementation of the Socio-cultural Resilience and Community Vitality Programme, and the Digital Transformation Programme, led by the GovTech",""],[1,"104","12","Socio-cultural Resilience and Community Vitality Programme","The Socio-cultural Resilience and Community Vitality programme aims to strengthen Bhutan's resilience to various risks that could undermine its stability, progress and well-being, through the comprehensive management of emerging and imminent threat perceptions.",""],[1,"107","2","Bhutanese Core Values and Cultural Heritage Promotion","The nurturing and promotion of Bhutanese core values and principles will be carried out through multifaceted efforts.",""],[1,"107","3","Cultural Heritage Conservation and Restoration Programme","The construction and restoration of dzongs, lhakhangs and other cultural institutions will contribute to preserving tangible cultural heritage.",""],[1,"107","3","Youth Engagement in Cultural Custodianship Initiative","To this end, the younger generation will be engaged as custodians of tangible and intangible culture through innovative means.",""],[1,"107","3","Cultural Professions Certification and Private Sector Engagement","This will be leveraged as a mainstream profession by engaging the private sector, and by certifying local professionals, artisans and artists.",""],[1,"107","4","Digitisation of Cultural and Religious Events","Efforts to uphold and promote Bhutan's intangible cultural heritage will include the digitisation of cultural and religious events, creation of a conducive environment for custodians of spiritual heritage, engagement of local governments and communities in fostering community vitality, and engagement of the younger generation in local culture and language through digital technology.",""],[1,"107","4","Supportive Environment for Custodians of Spiritual Heritage","Efforts to uphold and promote Bhutan's intangible cultural heritage will include the digitisation of cultural and religious events, creation of a conducive environment for custodians of spiritual heritage, engagement of local governments and communities in fostering community vitality, and engagement of the younger generation in local culture and language through digital technology.",""],[1,"107","4","Community Vitality and Local Government Engagement Initiative","Efforts to uphold and promote Bhutan's intangible cultural heritage will include the digitisation of cultural and religious events, creation of a conducive environment for custodians of spiritual heritage, engagement of local governments and communities in fostering community vitality, and engagement of the younger generation in local culture and language through digital technology.",""],[1,"107","4","Youth Engagement in Local Culture and Language","Efforts to uphold and promote Bhutan's intangible cultural heritage will include the digitisation of cultural and religious events, creation of a conducive environment for custodians of spiritual heritage, engagement of local governments and communities in fostering community vitality, and engagement of the younger generation in local culture and language through digital technology.",""]],"19":[[1,"125","4","Fiscal Management and Macroeconomic Policy Reform","To ensure robust management of the economy, the 13th FYP will see renewed focus on policy and institutional improvements in fiscal management, debt management, and monetary and liquidity management - with close monitoring of macroeconomic instabilities and exogenous shocks.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"125","4","Prudent Fiscal Policy Coordination and Resource Management","The Ministry of Finance will ensure prudent use of financial resources, formulate and coordinate economic policies, and formulate prudent and sustainable fiscal policies.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"125","4","Tax Reform and Medium-Term Revenue Strategy","Fiscal policy reforms will include tax reform, implementation of a medium-term revenue strategy, and improvements in macroeconomic modelling and forecasting.",""],[1,"125","6","Monetary Policy and Reserve Management Reform","The Royal Monetary Authority will undertake improvements in monetary policy and reserve management, by revisiting market-based policy framework and enhancing access to credit for productive sectors.",""],[1,"126","1","Macroeconomic Oversight and Monitoring of 13th FYP Economic Targets","the Governance Cluster will closely monitor and exercise oversight over the 13th FYP economic development targets to reduce youth unemployment, maintain inflation and reduce the trade deficit.",""],[1,"140","1","Medium-Term Revenue Strategy","To enhance domestic revenue mobilisation, a medium-term revenue strategy (MTRS) will be implemented, focusing on broadening the tax base to maintain a tax-to-GDP ratio above 15 percent and reviewing existing fiscal incentives and tax exemptions.",""]],"20":[[1,"140","4","Fiscal Deficit Financing Strategy","External borrowing will be the primary source of financing, with a focus on securing highly concessional funds from institutions including the Asian Development Bank (ADB) and the World Bank (WB).",""],[1,"140","4","Domestic Bond and Treasury Bill Financing","Additionally, domestic funds will be raised through government bonds and treasury bills to achieve a balanced strategy for meeting the fiscal deficit.",""]],"21":[[1,"19","7","Digital Transformation Programme","Under the Digital Transformation Programme, Bhutan seeks to strengthen its resilience against cyber threats while creating a secure and trustworthy digital",""],[1,"21","3","Transformational Governance Programme","The Transformational Governance Programme and the Digital Transformation Programme will collectively drive the effective implementation of the 13th FYP across all four clusters.",""],[1,"21","3","Digital Transformation Programme","The Transformational Governance Programme and the Digital Transformation Programme will collectively drive the effective implementation of the 13th FYP across all four clusters.",""],[1,"21","4","Data Ecosystem Improvement for Evidence-Based Decision-Making","The data ecosystem will be improved to support evidence-based decision-making",""],[1,"21","4","Digital Governance and Public Service Delivery Initiative","Digital technology will be leveraged and promoted for efficient governance and public services delivery",""],[1,"21","5","Digital Transformation Programme","The Digital Transformation Programme aims to position Bhutan as a digitally empowered and resilient society through four key strategies: 1) Promoting inclusive digital governance, 2) Building a thriving digital economy, 3) Cultivating a vibrant digital society, and 4) Investing in key enablers.",""],[1,"58","5","Digital Transformation Programme","All three programmes will leverage ICTs and will have components under the Digital Transformation Programme spearheaded by the GovTech Agency.",""],[1,"59","6","One-Stop Public Service Delivery Point","Government will also create a dedicated 'one-stop service delivery point' for all public services and businesses.",""],[1,"103","5","Digital Transformation Programme","The security cluster outputs across the two outcome areas will be delivered through the implementation of the Socio-cultural Resilience and Community Vitality Programme, and the Digital Transformation Programme, led by the GovTech",""],[1,"121","4","Transformational Governance Programme","The governance cluster outputs across the two outcome areas will be delivered through the implementation of the Transformational Governance Programme and the Digital Transformation Programme.",""],[1,"121","4","Digital Transformation Programme","The governance cluster outputs across the two outcome areas will be delivered through the implementation of the Transformational Governance Programme and the Digital Transformation Programme.",""],[1,"121","5","Transformational Governance Programme","The Transformational Governance Programme programme aims to transform governance by adopting a whole-of society approach, underpinned by agile and foresight-driven anticipatory governance mechanisms.",""],[1,"126","5","Digital Transformation Programme","This involves embracing digital transformation across sectors, implementing e-governance initiatives, and promoting digital connectivity - which will be facilitated by the GovTech Agency with the implementation of the Digital Transformation Programme.",""],[1,"126","6","Administrative Procedure Automation and Digitisation","Through automation and digitisation, administrative procedures will be streamlined to facilitate citizen engagement, and to enable public servants to focus on strategic decision-making and the delivery of high-quality services.",""],[1,"126","6","Artificial Intelligence and Data Analytics for Evidence-Based Governance","Emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence and data analytics will be leveraged to enable evidence-based decision-making, and to enhance the effectiveness of overall governance.",""],[1,"127","2","Digital Transformation Programme","Bhutan's Digital Transformation Programme will steer the nation towards becoming a high-income GNH economy by fostering digital governance, economy and society and investing in key enablers.",""],[1,"127","3","Digital Governance, Digital Economy, Digital Society, and Enablers Programme","The overall outlay for this programme is BTN. 10,000 million, of which BTN. 5,148.19 million will be invested in strengthening Digital Governance.",""],[1,"127","4","Digital Public Service Delivery Enhancement","Initiatives within public service delivery will prioritise the enhancement of efficiency and citizen satisfaction through technology-driven solutions.",""],[1,"127","4","Government Operations Transformation","Meanwhile, efforts to transform government operations will target the reduction of operational costs and the process optimisation.",""],[1,"127","4","Smart Governance and Open Data Initiative","Smart governance initiatives will underscore the importance of data-driven decision-making, citizen engagement, and open data initiatives.",""],[1,"127","5","Digital Governance Modernization Initiative","These collective initiatives aim to modernise governance practices, elevate service delivery standards, and empower citizens by fostering trust and confidence in digital governance.",""],[1,"129","1","Digital Governance and Digital Economy Enabling Investments","The government will prioritise investments in key enablers for implementing digital governance, fostering a thriving digital economy, and cultivating a vibrant digital society.",""],[1,"129","1","Digital Infrastructure Development","Digital infrastructure is foundational for connectivity ensuring accessibility, affordability, and reliability.",""],[1,"129","1","Technology Adoption for Public Sector Efficiency and Productivity","Besides infrastructure development, cutting-edge technologies will be embraced to drive efficiency gains, enhance services, and boost productivity across sectors.",""],[1,"157","10","Autonomous Digital Transformation Agency","An autonomous agency mandated to drive digital transformation to enhance the effectiveness and efficiency of the government, transform public services to be citizen- centric, and create a safe and thriving Bhutanese digital economy",""]],"22":[[1,"14","4","Business Ecosystem Improvement","the four key deliverables or outputs of the economic cluster are: 1) An improved business ecosystem",""],[1,"15","1","Private Sector Enabling Environment Reform","Private sector development and participation will be facilitated by creating a conducive environment for businesses to thrive and drive economic growth.",""],[1,"55","5","Business Environment Deregulation and Policy Harmonisation","An improved business ecosystem requires deregulation as well as harmonisation and implementation of strategic policies, and improvements in business services delivery.",""],[1,"59","2","Private Sector Development and Participation Facilitation","This programme aims to foster sustainable and inclusive economic growth by employing three key strategies: facilitating private sector development and participation, investing in strategic infrastructure and investing in traditional growth drivers as well as new sources of growth.",""],[1,"59","3","Private Sector-Led Growth Model Promotion","The 13th FYP will promote a conducive ecosystem that increasingly accommodates a greater role for private initiatives and allows diverse professions and activities to thrive.",""],[1,"59","4","Regulatory Streamlining and Simplification Reform","regulations will be streamlined, simplified and eliminated based on a comprehensive review of existing policies.",""],[1,"59","4","Regulatory Reform Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Monitoring and evaluation mechanisms will be put in place for continuous assessment of the impact of regulatory reforms.",""],[1,"59","4","Business-Friendly Sector Policy Amendments","Policies for energy, mining, environment, trade, competition, tourism and foreign direct investments, among others, will be amended to be more business friendly.",""],[1,"59","6","Business Regulatory Reform Package","It will be complemented by regulatory reforms to ease doing business, and every effort will be made to ensure that current electronic service portals work seamlessly.",""],[1,"60","1","Business Licensing and Tax Framework Reform","Reforms in business licensing and the tax framework will be undertaken, to allow specialisation or a focus on specific activities rather than businesses being importer, supplier and manufacturer all at once.",""],[1,"60","6","Business-Friendly Regulatory and Innovation Climate Reform","A business-friendly policy and regulatory climate, where innovation and privatisation will thrive, will be ensured.",""],[1,"66","2","Service Sector Regulatory and Infrastructure Reform","Promoting Bhutan as a destination for niche services requires regulatory reforms and infrastructure development for the service sector but other reforms as well, such as to immigration and labour permits to facilitate the movement of people.",""],[1,"144","2","Policy Barrier Removal and Public Service Streamlining","Meanwhile, it will allow the government to focus on building infrastructure for undisrupted connectivity, production and trade, as well as on removing policy barriers and streamlining public service delivery.",""]],"23":[[1,"14","5","Economic Transformation Programme","The Economic Transformation Programme aims to foster sustainable and inclusive growth through three key strategies.",""],[1,"37","1","Economic Transformation under the 13th FYP","Bhutan must seize the opportunity of the 13th FYP to re-balance GNH by focusing on economic transformation.",""],[1,"37","1","Partnership Mobilization for Economic Opportunities","It needs to be much more open and courageous in inviting partners to create better economic opportunities for its people.",""],[1,"58","5","Economic Transformation Programme","To deliver the four economic development outputs outlined above, three national programmes will be implemented: Economic Transformation, Twenty-first Century Skilling, and Ecological Diversity and Resilience.",""],[1,"59","5","Economic Development Board Reform and Investment Promotion Mechanism","The EDB will carry out necessary reforms in the economic and public sectors to debottleneck investment constraints, address policy conflicts pertaining to businesses, coordinate stakeholders, and monitor the delivery and performance of key players.",""],[1,"61","4","Investment in Traditional and New Growth Drivers","investments will continue to be made in traditional growth drivers as well as in new sources of growth.",""],[1,"61","4","Nine Focus Area Intervention Package","A range of interventions will be undertaken in the nine focus areas detailed below.",""]],"24":[[1,"43","5","Safe and Liveable Human Settlements Programme","we will ensure safe and liveable human settlement in all 20 Dzongkhags - characterised by equitable access to affordable housing, and efficient and affordable public transport and private healthcare",""],[1,"56","9","Human Settlements Liveability and Connectivity Improvement","The liveability of human settlements must be enhanced with reliable and affordable access to services and amenities.",""],[1,"61","3","National Capital Region and Linked Urban Centres Development","the liveability, safety and sustainability of human settlements will be enhanced by the creation of the National Capital Region (NCR) spanning across Thimphu and Paro, several Linked Urban Centres (LUC) spanning across the Phuentsholing-Samtse, Trongsa-Bumthang, Mongar-Trashigang and Samdrup Jongkhar-Nganglam regions, and the implementation of the Punakha- Wangduephodrang Regional Plan.",""],[1,"61","3","Infrastructure Development in Dzongkhag Urban Centres","Infrastructure development will also take place in areas falling outside the NCR and LUCs in Dzongkhag Urban Centres.",""]],"25":[[1,"14","4","Skilled Labour Force Development","the four key deliverables or outputs of the economic cluster are: 3) A skilled labour force",""],[1,"15","3","Twenty-first Century Skilling Programme","The Twenty-first Century Skilling Programme aims to equip the Bhutanese population with the necessary education and skills for the modern economy through initiatives in technical and vocational training (TVET), tertiary education and skilling, upskilling and reskilling programmes.",""],[1,"57","1","Skills Training, Certification, and Reskilling Programme","Solutions include training and certification, including reskilling of the domestic labour force for specific skills to match market demands, and upgrading their qualifications through courses relevant to the needs of the 21st century market.",""],[1,"57","2","Skilled and Certified Workforce Expansion","The number of appropriately skilled and certified Bhutanese workers in automobile, plumbing, electrical and construction works, among other vocations will have to increase.",""],[1,"57","2","Tertiary Qualification Expansion in Priority Professions","There also needs to be an increase in the Bhutanese labour force possessing tertiary qualifications in engineering, teaching, medicine and information and technology (ICT).",""],[1,"58","5","Twenty-first Century Skilling Programme","To deliver the four economic development outputs outlined above, three national programmes will be implemented: Economic Transformation, Twenty-first Century Skilling, and Ecological Diversity and Resilience.",""],[1,"66","6","Human Capital and Skills Development Programme","This programme is aimed at equipping the Bhutanese population with relevant knowledge and skill sets for 21st century economic needs.",""],[1,"67","2","21st Century Workforce Development Programme","Towards building a 21st century workforce, BTN 10,000 million will be invested through this programme.",""],[1,"67","3","Transformation of TEIs and TVET System","the transformation of TEIs and the TVET system is critical.",""],[1,"68","2","Youth Skills Development for Labour Market Integration","Under this programme, the priority is to provide youth with relevant skills for successful integration into the 21st century labour market.",""],[1,"68","2","Tertiary Education Restructuring and Diversification Reform","the tertiary education system has undergone major transformation, it still requires major restructuring and diversification of programmes - to elevate quality to match international standards and to align with demand in key economic sectors, including manufacturing, energy and environment, agriculture, mining, construction, tourism, the digital and creative industries, finance and banking, and social services such as health and education.",""],[1,"68","3","International University Partnership and Joint Programme Initiative","Tertiary Education Institutes will forge partnerships with reputed international universities to offer joint programmes, elective courses with credit transfer, and access to online courses to offer personalised learning options.",""],[1,"68","3","Undergraduate Scholarship Programme for Priority Areas","The government also remains committed to investing in undergraduate studies through scholarship programmes in priority areas, enabling students to study at top-tier international universities.",""],[1,"68","4","TVET Transformation Investment Programme","investment will be directed towards transforming TVET.",""],[1,"68","5","Targeted Short-Term Skills Training for Graduates","the government will invest in targeted short-term skills training, tailored to job-seekers who are fresh out of universities, to enhance thier employability while also supplying a skilled workforce to economic sectors.",""],[1,"68","6","Targeted Skills Training for Priority Economic Sectors","targeted skills training will be provided in priority economic sectors to the existing workforce who require upskilling and reskilling.",""],[1,"154","1","Skills Development and Entrepreneurship Programme","Entrepreneurship training and mentoring including setting up of a business incubation centers will be supported especially for youths.",""],[1,"154","2","Youth Employment Support and Affordable Education Credit","Target support for facilitating youth employment including affordable credit to support education and training.",""],[1,"158","3","National Gyalsung Programme","National Gyalsung Programme.",""]],"26":[[1,"62","5","Tourism Product Development for Authentic Visitor Experiences","efforts will focus on providing visitors with authentic uncontrived experiences that showcase the rich cultural heritage and natural beauty of Bhutan, by developing various tourism products.",""],[1,"62","6","Sustainable Tourism Partnerships and Responsible Travel Promotion","This will be done through partnerships with media and other platforms.",""],[1,"63","1","Tourism Promotion for Sustainable Development","Tourism will be promoted as a catalyst for sustainable development, generating economic opportunities while preserving Bhutan's cultural and natural heritage.",""],[1,"63","2","Tourism Promotion in Low-Arrival Dzongkhags","Special attention will be given to promoting tourism in Dzongkhags with fewer or no tourist arrivals, and to promote yearlong tourist arrival in Bhutan.",""],[1,"63","3","Support for International Film and Documentary Production","the production of international films and documentaries on culture, environment, lifestyle and Bhutanese arts and tradition will be supported.",""],[1,"63","4","Tourism Services Professionalisation Initiative","Efforts shall be doubled to professionalise tourism services by improving the quality and efficiency of visa, accommodation, transport, information and roadside amenities services.",""],[1,"63","5","Tourism Product Diversification and Marketing Strategy","By diversifying and enhancing tourism products and experiences, professionalising services, and implementing vigorous marketing strategies to attract new markets, the goal is to attract at least 300,000 tourists annually from diverse sources.",""],[1,"153","6","Tourism Development Support Measures","The measures would include providing affordable credit support to upscale lower-end hotels, support tourism marketing, enhancing existing products and developing new products.",""]],"27":[[1,"63","6","Accelerated Hydropower Investment Programme","Investments in this renewable energy source will therefore be accelerated, towards enhancing energy security and to support the development of domestic industries and the diversification of the economy.",""],[1,"63","6","Hydropower Project Completion and New Project Pipeline","The completion of ongoing hydropower projects and initiation of new projects will be complemented by the development of energy storage systems and other related infrastructure components.",""],[1,"63","6","Energy Storage and Related Infrastructure Development","The completion of ongoing hydropower projects and initiation of new projects will be complemented by the development of energy storage systems and other related infrastructure components.",""],[1,"63","7","Completion of Punatsangchhu-I and Punatsangchhu-II Hydropower Projects","In addition to prioritising the completion of the Punatsangchhu-I (1,200 MW) and Punatsangchhu-II (1,020 MW) 00hydropower projects, the government will initiate the following new large hydropower projects in the 13th FYP:",""],[1,"64","5","Lunana Mini Hydropower Project","Development of the 500 kW Lunana Mini Hydropower project",""],[1,"64","6","Gongri-Jericho Pumped Storage Project Construction","Completion of Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) for the 1800 MW Gongri-Jericho pumped storage project and commencement of construction",""]],"28":[[1,"56","10","Non-Hydropower Renewable Energy Expansion","Moreover, to improve the accessibility, reliability and affordability of energy, the harnessing of non-hydropower renewable energy, i.e. wind and solar power will be enhanced while reducing fossil fuel consumption.",""],[1,"64","7","Alternative Renewable Energy Development","Alternative renewable energy sources such as solar, wind, geothermal and biomass will be leveraged, to contribute to the energy mix and enhance energy security.",""],[1,"64","8","Utility-Scale Solar Power Development","Development of 500 MW utility-scale solar projects at various locations",""],[1,"64","9","Solar Energy Project Implementation Programme","Implementation of various solar projects including rooftop installations in urban and rural areas, prosumer models, agri-solar projects, rural energy supply projects, and solar thermal projects",""],[1,"64","11","1 MW Pilot Green Hydrogen Project","Implementation of a 1 MW pilot green hydrogen project",""]],"29":[[1,"64","13","National Geological and Mineral Resource Mapping Programme","Comprehensive geological and mineral resource mapping through nationwide magnetic, gravity, geochemical and metallic surveys",""]],"30":[[1,"60","4","Private Sector Participation Enhancement through Privatization, PPPs, and Outsourcing","Private sector participation will be enhanced through privatisation and divestment, public private partnerships (PPPs) and outsourcing.",""],[1,"60","5","Gradual SOE Privatization Programme","the government will encourage the gradual privatisation of those SOEs that could be operated more efficiently by the private sector",""],[1,"60","5","Private Sector Outsourcing of Government Services","Wherever feasible, government services will be outsourced to the private sector, including the construction and operation of facilities such as dry ports and industrial parks",""],[1,"60","6","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Delivery","PPPs will be pursued to enable the utilisation of private sector resources, expertise and innovation towards the provision of critical public infrastructure and services, with shared risks.",""],[1,"60","6","PPP Pilot Infrastructure Project Selection","The government will identify a few infrastructural projects to pursue through the PPP model, with the government's involvement to make it a success and for future replication.",""]],"31":[[1,"56","8","Export Market Expansion and Trade Relations Strengthening","Market access will be enhanced, particularly for the export of Bhutanese products.",""],[1,"56","8","Export Product and Service Development Support","This requires exploration and establishment of new markets; strengthened bilateral, multilateral and regional trade relations; and the development of new export products and services.",""],[1,"56","8","Industry and Start-up Support and Intellectual Property Facilitation","Moreover, new and existing industries and start-ups will require support and intellectual property registration will be facilitated.",""],[1,"65","5","Niche Services and Cultural Enterprise Development","Investment in niche services are geared towards bolstering areas of services and other industries that draw on Bhutan's spiritual, cultural and environmental wealth and its status as a peaceful country.",""],[1,"65","5","Local Culture and Traditional Knowledge for Cultural Enterprises","Efforts will be made to leverage local culture and traditional knowledge for cultural enterprises and assets.",""],[1,"65","5","Herbal Remedies and Zorig Chusum Product Development","Bhutan's potential in herbal-based natural remedies and medicines and zorig chusum arts and craft products, among others will be explored as niche products.",""]],"32":[[1,"15","4","Ecological Diversity and Resilience Programme","The Ecological Diversity and Resilience Programme underscores Bhutan's commitment to climate-resilient development and sustainability.",""],[1,"42","3","Sustainable Growth Programme","All programmes and activities to drive growth will be pursued within the imperatives of sustainability - including the constitutional mandate to maintain at least 60 percent of Bhutan under forest cover for all times, and its international commitment to remain carbon neutral in perpetuity.",""],[1,"42","3","International Cooperation for Sustainable Development","Through innovative approaches and deepened engagement with the international community, it will be more pragmatic in managing the co-benefits and trade-offs between growth outcomes and environmental conservation.",""],[1,"58","5","Ecological Diversity and Resilience Programme","To deliver the four economic development outputs outlined above, three national programmes will be implemented: Economic Transformation, Twenty-first Century Skilling, and Ecological Diversity and Resilience.",""],[1,"69","3","Ecological Diversity and Resilience Programme","the Ecological Diversity and Resilience Programme is aimed at ensuring Bhutan's pursuit of a low- carbon and climate-resilient development pathway and promoting green growth.",""],[1,"69","3","Implementation of Bhutan's Long-Term Low Greenhouse Gas Emission and Climate Resilient Development Strategy","This will involve the implementation of Bhutan's Long-Term Low Greenhouse Gas Emission and Climate Resilient Development Strategy (LTS), which anchors mitigation strategies and adaptation plans in key sectors.",""],[1,"69","5","Natural Resource Monetization and Carbon Market Participation","Through prudent management of natural resources and ecosystem services, Bhutan's environmental assets will be monetised to support economic development.",""],[1,"69","5","Carbon Market Participation Mechanism","Bhutan will participate in carbon markets as an important additional source of finance and investments.",""]],"33":[[1,"70","2","National Water Master Plan and River Basin Management Plans","Sustainable water resource management will be advanced with the development and implementation of a national water master plan and river basin management plans",""],[1,"70","2","Climate-Resilient Water Infrastructure Guidelines","guidelines on climate-resilient water infrastructure based on assessments of climate vulnerability and risk for priority water sectors",""],[1,"70","2","Water Resources Management Knowledge Bank","the institution of a knowledge bank on water resources management",""],[1,"70","2","Water Storage Development and Nature-Based Watershed Restoration","Avenues for potential natural and built water storage will be explored and developed, and suitable nature-based solutions for watershed conservation and restoration will be implemented",""],[1,"70","3","Water Services Payment Mechanisms","payment mechanisms will be established for water services",""],[1,"70","3","Water Investment Opportunity Exploration","investment opportunities will be explored",""],[1,"70","3","Groundwater and Recharge Area Assessment","Potential groundwater and recharge areas, and possible avenues for abstraction will be explored and assessed.",""],[1,"70","3","Water-Based Venture Development","Avenues for water-based ventures will be created",""],[1,"70","3","Water-Efficient Technology Promotion and Adoption","the promotion and adoption of emerging water-efficient and innovative technologies.",""]],"34":[[1,"70","5","Climate Data Aggregation and Environmental Monitoring Systems","This also involves the aggregation of climate data, the development of a natural capital accounting system and the digitisation of Bhutan's National Carbon Registry.",""],[1,"70","5","Automated Air-Quality Monitoring System Strengthening","It will also require strengthening automated air-quality monitoring systems and infrastructure, ensuring at least 10 percent implementation of the National Adaptation Plan (NAP), alongside a cumulative emission reduction of 12,507.36 gigagrams (Gg) carbon (CO2e) dioxide by 2030.",""],[1,"70","5","Climate and Environmental Scientific Museum Establishment","Moreover, a climate and environmental scientific museum will be established.",""]],"35":[[1,"16","4","Health System Strengthening and Governance Reform","The seven key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 3) Improved access to quality health and health-related services and products, 4) An adequate and competent health workforce, 5) A sustainable health financing system and innovative governance, 6) A strengthened regulatory, monitoring and health security system, and 7) Information and technology harnessed to enhance health system efficiency.",""],[1,"17","2","Healthy Drukyul Programme","The Healthy Drukyul Programme aims to ensure the good health and well-being of the Bhutanese population through three key strategies to achieve universal health coverage, promote healthier lifestyles and improve healthcare accessibility and quality.",""],[1,"17","3","Health Workforce and Service Delivery Improvement","Health governance and healthcare delivery services will be improved by enhancing the health workforce, ensuring access to medical supplies and equipment, and streamlining patient referral pathways.",""],[1,"17","3","Digital Health Regulatory and Monitoring Systems","Innovative approaches and digital solutions will be leveraged to improve regulatory and monitoring systems.",""],[1,"17","3","Preventive and Promotive Healthcare Investment","Investments will be made in cost-effective preventive and promotive healthcare with an emphasis on proactive health risk identification, promoting healthy lifestyles, and combating NCDs through evidence-based interventions.",""],[1,"17","3","Digital Health Capacity Enhancement","Digital health capabilities will be enhanced to strengthen healthcare services and surveillance.",""],[1,"45","2","Robust Health Services and Social Security Interventions","robust health services and social security interventions",""],[1,"66","1","Integrated Health Services with Traditional and Mental Health Care","It will also include the provision of health services that integrate traditional medicine, astrology services, and mental health services.",""],[1,"79","3","Preventive and Curative Healthcare Services Expansion","This includes providing preventive and curative healthcare services, and enhancing the effectiveness of the health governance system through sustainable health financing and universal health coverage.",""],[1,"79","3","Health Governance Strengthening through Sustainable Financing and Universal Coverage","This includes providing preventive and curative healthcare services, and enhancing the effectiveness of the health governance system through sustainable health financing and universal health coverage.",""],[1,"79","3","Population Behaviour Change for Health Improvement","Moreover, promoting behavioural changes in the population is necessary to support physical, mental and psychosocial health improvements.",""],[1,"79","4","Healthy Lifestyle Promotion for NCD Prevention","More Bhutanese will be encouraged to practise healthy lifestyles to minimise NCD risk factors including tobacco use, harmful consumption of alcohol and areca nut, physical inactivity and unhealthy diets.",""],[1,"79","6","Investment in Specialist Healthcare Services","This involves investing in appropriate and quality sub- and super-specialist services within Bhutan, and ensuring equitable distribution of quality healthcare services to alleviate financial burdens and to provide timely access to quality healthcare.",""],[1,"80","1","Health Workforce Capacity Building","This requires building a well-capacitated workforce to meet long-term needs, especially for specialised tertiary services.",""],[1,"80","2","Sustainable Health Financing and Financial Protection Measures","This involves greater public investment, reduced out-of-pocket (OOPs) spending on total health expenditure, and alternative mechanisms for sustainable health financing and enhanced financial protection, with a stronger emphasis on preventive healthcare.",""],[1,"80","4","Expansion of ICT-Enabled Healthcare Systems","This requires expansion of ICT-enabled healthcare solutions such as the Hospital Information System (HIS), electronic Patient Information System (ePIS), and eBMSIS for medical product procurement and distribution, guided by the e-health strategy.",""],[1,"80","5","Healthy Drukyul Programme","The Healthy Drukyul Programme (HDP), with a budget of BTN 20,000 million, is dedicated to ensuring the good health and well-being of the Bhutanese population.",""],[1,"81","2","Health Governance and Service Delivery Improvement Programme","The programme will employ three key strategies: improving health governance system and healthcare delivery services, investing in cost-effective preventive and promotive healthcare, and rationalising health facilities for improved service delivery.",""],[1,"81","3","Health Services Management and Expansion","The Ministry of Health and the National Medical Services collectively seek to address the health needs of the population through improved clinical services management and need-based expansion of essential and specialised health services.","Ministry of Health | National Medical Services"],[1,"81","3","Health Governance and Quality Improvement Reform","Enhancing overall health services primarily involves improving the health governance system and quality of healthcare services delivery, with the goal to attain universal health coverage.",""],[1,"81","4","Health Workforce Professional Development and Retention Initiative","Investments will be prioritised for professional development through upskilling and skills development.",""],[1,"81","4","Supportive Health Workplace and Career Advancement Measures","Efforts will be made to create supportive work environments that promote work-life balance and foster career advancement to retain skilled professionals.",""],[1,"81","5","Medical Supplies, Vaccines, and Equipment Maintenance Prioritization","The timely access to medical supplies and vaccines, and functionality and upkeep of medical equipment in all health facilities will be prioritised.",""],[1,"81","5","Patient Referral Pathway Streamlining","Patient referral pathways will be streamlined to make the most of the existing health facilities in Bhutan.",""],[1,"81","5","People-Centred Healthcare Innovation and Health Financing Reform","Concerted efforts will be made towards adopting innovative approaches to high-quality people-centred healthcare services, and the creation of an equity- based sustainable health financing ecosystem.",""],[1,"81","6","ICT-Based Health Regulatory and Monitoring Improvement","ICT-based digital solutions will be leveraged to improve the regulatory, monitoring and health security environment, which will also include regulation of Sorig wellness services.",""],[1,"81","6","Private Sector Participation in Health Services","The potential for private sector involvement in the health sector will be explored as an additional option, while maintaining high-quality public health services for citizens.",""],[1,"81","7","Preventive and Promotive Healthcare Investment Prioritization","investments in preventive and promotive healthcare will be prioritised.",""],[1,"82","1","Immunisation and Health Screening Programme","interventions such as immunisations and health screenings, promotion of healthy lifestyles, and combating NCDs.",""],[1,"82","1","Healthy Lifestyle Promotion Initiative","interventions such as immunisations and health screenings, promotion of healthy lifestyles, and combating NCDs.",""],[1,"82","1","Non-Communicable Disease Control Measures","interventions such as immunisations and health screenings, promotion of healthy lifestyles, and combating NCDs.",""],[1,"82","2","Whole-of-Society Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","a whole of society approach will be adopted towards ensuring a supportive environment for people to engage in healthy habits.",""],[1,"83","1","Digital Health Capability Enhancement","Digital health capabilities will be enhanced to strengthen health information and communication for improved healthcare services.",""],[1,"83","2","NCD Risk Reduction and Disease Management Measures","Evidence-based interventions will be made to reduce other NCD risk factors and to manage diseases.",""],[1,"83","3","Reproductive, Maternal, Newborn, Child and Adolescent Health Services Enhancement","Interventions will also be enhanced for reproductive, maternal, new-born, child and adolescent health;",""],[1,"83","3","Infectious Disease Prevention, Control and Elimination Measures","the prevention, control and elimination of infectious diseases;",""],[1,"83","3","Antimicrobial Resistance Protection Measures","and to safeguard communities from the devastating impact of antimicrobial resistance.",""]],"36":[[1,"17","2","Need-Based Rationalisation of Health Facilities","Need-based rationalisation of health facilities will be conducted to enhance accessibility and quality of healthcare while optimising resources.",""],[1,"17","2","Health Facility Construction and Consolidation","This includes constructing new hospitals and adjusting and consolidating existing facilities based on population needs ,and infrastructure improvements.",""],[1,"83","4","Need-Based Rationalisation of Health Facilities","a need-based rationalisation of health facilities will be carried out",""],[1,"83","5","Healthcare Infrastructure Expansion and Rationalisation","This strategic consolidation and expansion of healthcare infrastructure will include the construction of the Thimphu District Hospital, a National Cancer and Transplant Centre at the Jigme Dorji Wangchuck National Referral Hospital in Thimphu, and a Mother and Child Hospital in Monggar.",""],[1,"83","5","Health Facility Rationalisation Based on Service Needs","In other places, parameters such as disease burden, population migration rate, the changing size of catchment populations and improvement in road networks will be considered to rationalise health facilities so that resources can be prioritised based on needs.",""]],"37":[[1,"80","3","Strengthening Medicines, Food, and Medical Product Regulatory Systems","This requires existing monitoring and regulatory systems to be strengthened to ensure that medicines, vaccines, and biological and medical devices meet high standards and are safe, and that food products are safe for consumption.",""],[1,"80","3","Controlled Substances and Tobacco Offence Reduction Measures","Regulatory measures are also needed to reduce offences related to controlled substances and tobacco products.",""],[1,"80","3","Quality Assurance and Certification System Enhancement","Investment in quality assurance and certification systems will be enhanced to improve plant and animal biosecurity.",""]],"38":[[1,"16","5","Education Workforce Strengthening","The seven key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 1) Adequate, competent and motivated education professionals",""],[1,"16","5","Safe and Inclusive Education Infrastructure Improvement","The seven key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 2) Safe, inclusive and quality education infrastructure and facilities",""],[1,"16","5","Curriculum and Assessment System Reform","The seven key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 3) A dynamic and adaptive curriculum and assessment system",""],[1,"16","5","Learner and Educator Health and Well-Being Support","The seven key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 4) Improved health and well-being of learners and educators",""],[1,"16","5","Innovative Education Financing Mechanisms","The seven key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 5) Innovative financing mechanisms for education",""],[1,"16","5","Higher Education Policy and Innovation Support","The seven key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 6) Increased contribution to policy and innovation by higher education institutions",""],[1,"16","5","Lifelong Learning and Skills Development Opportunities","The seven key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 7) Lifelong learning and skills development opportunities",""],[1,"17","4","Early Childhood Care and Development Access Expansion","Access to early childhood care and development will be provided to all children aged 3 to 5;",""],[1,"17","4","Curriculum Modernization and STEM Education Reform","Curriculum and education programmes will be transformed by adopting curricula that align with global standards, focusing on science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) education, and fostering critical thinking.",""],[1,"17","5","Teacher Professional Development and Faculty Qualification Upgrade","The education workforce will be transformed by prioritising teacher professional development, upgrading faculty qualifications, and recruiting international academics to improve teaching quality and methodology.",""],[1,"17","5","Education Infrastructure Modernisation and School Consolidation","Investments will be made in building fit-for-purpose infrastructure, which will include modernising school infrastructure, establishing early childhood development centres, consolidating existing schools into centres of excellence, and improving digital infrastructure for teaching and learning.",""],[1,"18","1","Tertiary and TVET Governance Strengthening","Education governance will be enhanced by strengthening governance for tertiary and TVET institutions, and promoting functional autonomy for TVET.",""],[1,"18","1","Assessment and Certification System Enhancement","This will also include enhancing assessment and certification systems, and facilitating private sector participation for improved service quality and financial sustainability.",""],[1,"18","1","Private Sector Participation for Education Service Quality","This will also include enhancing assessment and certification systems, and facilitating private sector participation for improved service quality and financial sustainability.",""],[1,"18","1","Holistic Learning Environment Support","Additionally, to create a holistic learning environment, interventions will include enhancing sanitation facilities, sports engagement, and nutritional programmes.",""],[1,"45","2","Quality Education and Skills Development System","Bhutan aims to ensure the provision of quality education and skills development",""],[1,"66","1","International Campus Establishment and Holistic Services Initiative","This will involve the establishment of international campuses in Bhutan, provision of spiritual education and training, and courses focusing on conservation and climate change.",""],[1,"84","5","Fit-for-Purpose Education Infrastructure Development","Build fit-for- purpose infrastructures for schools, TVET and TEIS",""],[1,"84","6","Curriculum Revamp for ECCD, School, TVET, and Higher Education","Revamp ECCD and school curriculum, TVET and higher education programs .",""],[1,"84","7","Education Governance System Strengthening","Strengthen education governance system.",""],[1,"84","8","Short-Term Skilling, Re-skilling, and Upskilling Programs","Enhance short-term skilling, re-skilling, and upskilling programs.",""],[1,"85","4","Special Education and Inclusive Education Reform Package","urgent reforms are needed, such as updating curricula, building teacher competence, improving school infrastructure, improving the health and well-being of learners, and the overall transformation of the education governance system.",""],[1,"86","3","Education System Transformation Programme","Achieving this outcome requires a comprehensive transformation of Bhutan's education system, encompassing infrastructure quality, utilisation of digital technology, teacher competencies, curriculum and assessment benchmarked to international standards, and clear pathways from school to TVET and tertiary education.",""],[1,"86","3","Innovative Education Financing Mechanisms","It also underscores a need to leverage innovative financing mechanisms for the long- term sustainability of the education system.",""],[1,"86","5","Education Professional Capacity Strengthening","This requires strengthening the capacities of education professionals across all levels, from ECCD centres to tertiary institutions, including TVET institutes and SEN schools.",""],[1,"86","5","ICT and Digital Skills Training for Educators","Educators and instructors need to be equipped with essential skills, such as ICT and digital proficiency and student safety and protection",""],[1,"86","7","Curriculum and Assessment Alignment to International Standards","the school curriculum and assessment system and higher education programmes will need to be aligned to selected international standards.",""],[1,"86","7","Accreditation of TVET and Tertiary Education Institutions","Additionally, it requires accreditation of TVET and tertiary education institutes",""],[1,"86","7","Graduate Employability Enhancement Initiative","and enhancing graduates' employability.",""],[1,"87","1","Safe and Supportive Learning Environment Initiative","This is about creating secure and supportive learning environments, ensuring access to safe, clean drinking water, providing nutritious meals where needed, establishing effective mechanisms to prevent and address all forms of violence, engaging students in community service initiatives like the school scouts programme, promoting active participation in sports for physical health, and ensuring overall student satisfaction with campus life.",""],[1,"87","2","Innovative Education Financing Mechanisms","This entails establishing and sustaining innovative financing mechanisms, which can fund enhancing education governance and transforming the system.",""],[1,"87","2","International School Establishment and Standards Upgrade","This includes establishing international schools, upgrading programmes and courses to meet international standards, attracting international students, and promoting active participation from individuals and organisations in supporting the development of education.",""],[1,"87","3","University Research, Consultancy, and Extension Engagement Programme","This requires universities and institutes to generate high-impact research outputs, and to actively participate in meaningful consultancy, collaborative research and extension programmes aimed at practical application and societal impact.",""],[1,"87","4","Adult Education and Training Participation Expansion","This requires implementing interventions to broaden participation in adult education and training programmes to reskill and upskill, enhancing adult literacy rates, certifying professional qualifications from the various institutes, and providing opportunities for both in-service and pre-service students to pursue undergraduate or postgraduate programmes.",""],[1,"87","5","Education Transformation Programme","The Education Transformation Programme (EdTP) is aimed at fundamentally improving the Bhutanese education system and enhancing learning outcomes.",""],[1,"88","1","School Education System Transformation Strategy","Interventions to transform the school education system are grouped under four key strategies: transforming curriculum and programmes across all levels of education, transforming the educational workforce, building fit-for purpose infrastructure and enhancing education governance.","Ministry of Education and Skills Development (MoESD)"],[1,"88","2","Curriculum Modernization for Schools and Tertiary Institutions","Bhutanese schools and tertiary institutions will adopt and impart curricula that ensures quality education, aligns with global best practices and prepares students for diverse opportunities.",""],[1,"88","3","ECCD Curriculum Development and School Curriculum Reform","This includes developing the ECCD curriculum, revamping the school curriculum with a focus on transforming STEM education and learning resources, and benchmarking the curriculum to international standards.",""],[1,"88","4","Tertiary Education Institute Empowerment Programme","Tertiary Education Institutes (TEIs) will be empowered to enhance their contribution to evidence-based policy making, and to provide platforms for the creation and dissemination of knowledge.",""],[1,"88","4","Curriculum Restructuring and Upgrading to International Standards","Within the tertiary education system, programmes and courses will be restructured and upgraded to international standards and aligned to emerging job market needs.",""],[1,"88","4","International University Collaboration and Joint Degree Initiative","Collaborations will be undertaken with reputed international universities to facilitate joint degree programmes and elective courses with credit transfer, establish accreditation for flagship programmes to enhance their global recognition, and increase access to personalised learning solutions for students.",""],[1,"88","5","TVET Curriculum Reform and Quality Improvement","The TVET curriculum will also undergo significant reform, diversifying courses to meet industry demand.",""],[1,"88","5","TVET Institute Upgrading through International Partnerships","TVET institutes will be elevated to global standards through collaborations and partnerships with international TVET partners.",""],[1,"89","1","Curriculum Revamp for Essential Skills","curriculum will be revamped to impart essential skills beyond merely improving the literacy rate.",""],[1,"89","2","Teacher Professional Development Training Programme","both short-term and long-term professional development training for teachers - including those specialising in Special Educational Needs (SEN), ECCD, NFE, school counselling, and sports instruction - will be pursued.",""],[1,"89","2","Teacher Research Culture Promotion Initiative","Also to be promoted is a research culture to continuously improve teaching methodologies and enhance learning outcomes.",""],[1,"89","3","Faculty Qualification Upgrading and Professional Development Programme","Similarly, upgrading faculty qualifications is essential for delivering quality education programmes by Tertiary Education Institutes.",""],[1,"89","3","International Academic Recruitment for Tertiary Education Institutes","Tertiary Education Institutes will also recruit international academics as teachers and external examiners, to develop and review programmes and courses where national faculty expertise is lacking.",""],[1,"89","4","School Infrastructure Modernisation","Modernising school infrastructure is essential to enhancing inclusiveness and safety and creating a conducive environment for teaching and learning.",""],[1,"89","4","Early Childhood Development Centre Expansion","The 13th FYP will renew efforts to establish community, workplace and private ECCD centres to ensure equitable access to quality and inclusive services.",""],[1,"89","5","School Consolidation and Educational Excellence Centers","the focus will be on consolidating the 63 existing central schools and other larger schools where feasible, and transforming them into centres of educational excellence with improved infrastructure and facilities meeting global standards.",""],[1,"89","6","School Repurposing into Specialized Schools","some schools will be repurposed into specialised schools for STEM, Music and Arts, TVET, Sports and Rehabilitation and Recovery.",""],[1,"89","6","Digital School Infrastructure Upgrade","Strengthening digital infrastructure to enhance teaching and learning will be at the core of infrastructure development projects.",""],[1,"90","1","Inclusive and Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure and Teacher Housing Access","infrastructure including making it more inclusive and disaster-resilient, and will enhance access to affordable low-cost housing facilities for teachers.",""],[1,"90","2","Tertiary Education Infrastructure and Learning Environment Improvement","improving the quality and ensuring fit-for-purpose infrastructure of Tertiary Education Institutes will involve creating technology-driven learning environments.",""],[1,"90","3","Strengthening Governance of Tertiary and TVET Institutions","Governance of both tertiary and TVET institutions will be strengthened.",""],[1,"90","3","Innovative Revenue Generation Models for Tertiary Education Institutes","Tertiary Education Institutes will adopt new and innovative business models for revenue generation to bolster their financial sustainability.",""],[1,"90","3","Private Sector Participation in Sustainable Education Financing","An enabling environment will facilitate private sector participation in instituting innovative and sustainable financing mechanisms.",""],[1,"90","4","Assessment and Certification System Strengthening","assessment and certification systems will be strengthened to enhance the credibility of qualifications across all levels, and to promote excellence and accountability within the education system.",""],[1,"90","4","School Health and Well-Being Services Package","essential health and well-being services will be provided.",""],[1,"90","4","School WASH, Scouting, Sports, and Feeding Programmes","These include improving water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) facilities, promoting scouting, strengthening sporting and youth engagement, and enhancing school feeding and nutritional programmes.",""],[1,"90","4","School Sports Culture and Health Screening Collaboration","The Ministry of Education and Skills Development will also collaborate with the Bhutan Olympic Committee in promoting sports culture in schools and with the Ministry of Health to ensure periodic health screening.","Ministry of Education and Skills Development | Bhutan Olympic Committee | Ministry of Health"]],"39":[[1,"17","1","Shock-Responsive Inclusive Social Protection System","Outcome-3 focuses on establishing an operational shock-responsive, inclusive and comprehensive social protection system by 2029.",""],[1,"17","1","Enabling Environment for Comprehensive Social Protection","The three key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 1) An enabling environment for comprehensive social protection,",""],[1,"17","1","Expansion of Essential Social Protection Programmes","2) Strengthened and expanded essential social protection programmes,",""],[1,"17","1","Sustainable Population Scenario Maintenance","3) Maintaining a sustainable population scenario.",""],[1,"18","2","Comprehensive Social Protection System","a comprehensive social protection system will be established to foster a healthy and productive society by formulating policy frameworks and implementing interoperable welfare information management systems",""],[1,"18","2","Inclusive Social Protection Schemes for Disadvantaged Groups","Inclusive and sustainable social protection schemes will be introduced for the disadvantaged",""],[1,"18","2","Provident Fund and Non-Contributory Benefit Expansion","provident fund and non-contributory benefits will be expanded",""],[1,"18","2","Disability Inclusion Advancement","disability inclusion will be advanced",""],[1,"43","5","Universal Social Protection Expansion","we will have ensured that by 2034 all Bhutanese have access to comprehensive social protection mechanisms and services across the life-cycle, particularly for the most vulnerable.",""],[1,"45","4","Diaspora and Community Vitality Support","the stability and vitality of Bhutanese communities both home and abroad, and the vibrancy of our cultural heritage.",""],[1,"92","2","Kidu Social Protection Programme","His Majesty the King's Kidu programme serves as a crucial social protection mechanism, providing a robust safety net for the Bhutanese people.",""],[1,"92","6","Social Protection System Establishment","In the 13th FYP, the government aims to establish a social protection system that systematically addresses pressing social protection and welfare issues.",""],[1,"93","1","Social Protection Policy","a comprehensive Social Protection Policy, defining programmes, target groups and the funding modality.",""],[1,"93","2","Expansion of Social Insurance and Support Schemes","This requires increasing the coverage and premium of national life insurance, as well as the coverage of pension and provident schemes.",""],[1,"93","2","Development of New Social Protection Mechanisms","New systems or mechanisms need to be developed and instituted, which may include schemes for support for families, unemployment, emergencies and disaster response, unpaid care work, among others.",""],[1,"93","4","Comprehensive Social Security System Development","Thus, the necessary policy and legislative framework will be formulated and adopted and a key aspect will be creating an interoperable welfare information management system.","Cabinet Secretariat"],[1,"93","5","Inclusive Shock-Responsive Social Protection Schemes","Relevant agencies will introduce inclusive, sustainable and shock-responsive schemes to support all Bhutanese citizens, particularly the most vulnerable.",""],[1,"93","6","Implementation of the National Policy for Persons with Disabilities Action Plan","the action plan for the National Policy for Persons with Disabilities 2019 will be taken forward.",""],[1,"116","4","Affordable Housing Initiative","there are several initiatives such as providing affordable housing",""],[1,"116","4","Social Protection Scheme for Vulnerable Persons","instituting social protection schemes for vulnerable persons",""],[1,"116","4","Poverty-Based Local Government Resource Allocation","ensuring adequate resources for locations with high poverty incidence by using poverty as a criterion for local government resource allocation",""],[1,"154","3","Affordable Home Ownership Loan Support","Support home ownership through affordable loans for home ownership.",""]],"40":[[1,"34","3","Cross-cutting Inclusion Mainstreaming through Laws, Policies, and Systems","Cross-cutting themes including gender equality and empowerment and, disability inclusion, continue to be promoted and strengthened through relevant laws, policies and systems.",""],[1,"126","3","Integration of GECCDP and Social Inclusion into Cluster and Local Government Plans","The Cabinet Secretariat through the OCASC will ensure that all relevant themes are taken into consideration, making it a prerequisite for the four clusters and local governments to integrate GECCDP and other social inclusion concerns as relevant to their plans and programmes.","Cabinet Secretariat | OCASC"],[1,"126","4","Capacity Building for Integration Implementation","it will be important to ensure that the various agencies and local governments have the capacity to carry out the integration process with its associated implications on budgetary and other implementation details.",""],[1,"126","4","Cross-Sector Coordination and Civil Society Collaboration Mechanism","coordination and collaboration across sectors and with relevant civil society organisations will be facilitated.",""]],"41":[[1,"19","2","Effective and Efficient Border Management","The five key deliverables or outputs towards achieving this outcome are: 1) Effective and efficient border management,",""],[1,"19","5","Border Management Infrastructure and Systems Upgrade","Border management infrastructure and systems will be upgraded and enhanced to improve security and facilitate trade.",""],[1,"100","2","Border Management and Transboundary Security Strengthening","The 13th FYP shall ensure effective mitigation and management of security threats by enhancing border management and addressing transboundary issues, maintaining internal law and order, and by strengthening cyber security.",""],[1,"100","4","Border Management Strengthening and Immigration Automation","Border management will be strengthened to safeguard national interest and sovereignty.",""],[1,"105","16","Border Management Infrastructure Upgrade","Border management will be strengthened by upgrading essential infrastructure and instituting efficient systems and practices along key border areas.",""],[1,"105","16","Municipal Boundary Protection Walls and Integrated Check Posts","Municipal boundary protection walls and integrated check posts will be constructed and/or maintained",""],[1,"105","16","Regional Immigration Office Construction in Nanglam","A Regional Immigration Office will be constructed in Nanglam.",""],[1,"105","16","Border Management System Deployment","A Border Management System will be deployed",""],[1,"105","16","Border Security and Surveillance Equipment Installation","essential security and surveillance equipment will be installed where required.",""],[1,"105","17","Automated Immigration Clearance at Border Entry Points","Immigration clearance will be automated at key border entry points, embedding all immigration permits with QR codes.",""],[1,"105","17","Rapid Response System for Immigration Offences","A rapid response system to address immigration offences will be established.",""],[1,"106","1","Border Control Agency and Community Coordination for Immigration Management","various border control agencies as well as local communities will be promoted, towards improving immigration procedures, preventing illegal activities and safeguarding territorial integrity.",""]],"42":[[1,"19","2","Law and Order Maintenance","2) Maintaining law and order,",""],[1,"19","5","Preventive and Rehabilitative Programmes","Preventive and rehabilitative programmes will be instituted along with modernisation of law enforcement to reduce criminal activity.",""],[1,"19","5","Law Enforcement Modernisation","Preventive and rehabilitative programmes will be instituted along with modernisation of law enforcement to reduce criminal activity.",""],[1,"100","5","Community Safety and Crime Reduction Measures","This is about ensuring the safety of Bhutanese communities through crime reduction, drug-free society initiatives and measures to enhance fire safety, traffic and prison management.",""],[1,"100","5","Security Mechanisms and Crime Reporting System","It requires instituting security mechanisms, along with ensuring easy and robust crime reporting and registration mechanisms, among others.",""],[1,"106","5","Community Safety and Crime Reduction Measures","Community vitality will be enhanced by reducing criminal activity and improving public safety.",""],[1,"106","5","Fire Risk Mitigation and Road Safety Improvement","To safeguard lives and property, priority will be given to mitigating the risks of fire-related incidents and promoting safer roads and reducing accidents.",""],[1,"106","5","Drug Abuse Prevention, Treatment, Rehabilitation and Enforcement Strategy","With 'crime reduction and a drug-free society' being a key priority, a combination of prevention, treatment, rehabilitation and enforcement strategies will be employed to address the issues associated with drug abuse and addiction.",""],[1,"106","6","Reformatory Prison Management and Offender Rehabilitation Programme","Reformatory programmes will be institutionalised along with humane prison management practices, to reform offenders and reduce recidivism rates.",""]],"43":[[1,"19","2","Critical Infrastructure Protection","3) Securing critical infrastructure,",""],[1,"19","2","Disaster-Resilient Institutions and Communities","4) Disaster-resilient institutions and communities,",""],[1,"19","5","Disaster and Emergency Preparedness and Response Plans","Disaster and emergency response and preparedness plans will be instituted, including building capacities and establishing or securing critical infrastructure.",""],[1,"45","5","Disaster and Emergency Management and Critical Infrastructure Protection","It also entails effective management of disasters and other emergency situations, and ensuring connectivity as well as the protection of critical infrastructure - not only to facilitate disaster and emergency response, but also to enhance economic security.",""],[1,"98","2","Infrastructure Resilience Planning and Investment","There is therefore a need for comprehensive planning, risk management and investment in infrastructure resilience - in order to mitigate potential hazards and threats to critical road networks, power grids and fuel storage facilities, water and sewerage systems, communications systems, emergency services, financial institutions, and hospitals.",""],[1,"99","5","Strategic Relief Item Storage and Emergency Logistics Strengthening","There is urgent need to establish and store core relief items at strategic locations across Bhutan, in addition to improving connectivity and other measures to strengthen emergency logistics preparedness.",""],[1,"100","2","Disaster and Emergency Resilience Strengthening","Simultaneously, it will strengthen the resilience of institutions and communities to disasters and emergency situations by securing critical infrastructure, and through the sustainable management of natural resources.",""],[1,"100","6","Local Disaster Risk Reduction Strategy Implementation","the adoption and implementation of local disaster risk reduction strategies by Dzongkhags and critical agencies",""],[1,"100","6","Incident Command System and Coordination Mechanisms","the institution of functional Incident Command System and coordination mechanisms at all administrative levels (Dzongkhag, Thromdes and Gewogs)",""],[1,"100","6","Disaster Response Team Training Programme","trained disaster response teams in Dzongkhags and key agencies",""],[1,"100","6","Community Disaster Mitigation Preparedness and Response Training","regular training of communities on disaster mitigation, preparedness and response",""],[1,"100","6","National Emergency Management and Contingency Plan Operationalisation","the operationalisation of a national emergency management and contingency plan by 2025",""],[1,"101","2","Critical Supplies Provision for Emergency Needs","This deliverable will also ensure supply of critical energy, essential food items and medical food.",""],[1,"105","5","Disaster and Emergency Response Preparedness Plans","Instituting response and preparedness plans for disasters and emergencies",""],[1,"106","2","National Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Strengthening","A systematic approach will be taken to build Bhutan's preparedness and strengthen its resilience to disasters and all emergency situations.",""],[1,"106","2","Critical Energy, Food, and Medical Supply Continuity Policy","A national policy or guideline will be developed to ensure the availability of critical energy, food, medical supplies and other essentials.",""],[1,"106","3","Humanitarian Staging Areas and National Emergency Response System","Disaster response capacities will be built with the establishment of humanitarian staging areas in strategic locations, a single national 24/7 emergency helpline centre, a National Emergency Operation Centre (NEOC) in the capital, and a fully functional and resourced multisectoral disaster response team.",""],[1,"106","3","Multi-Hazard Risk Decision Support System Operationalisation","The Multi Hazard Risk Decision Support System (MHRDSS) will be operationalised and simulation exercises will be conducted.",""],[1,"106","4","Disaster Management Capacity Strengthening","The capacities of Disaster Management Committees (DMC), local government entities, simulation facilitators, and Search and Rescue (SAR) teams will be built and strengthened for efficient coordination.",""],[1,"106","4","Community Preparedness and Early Warning Enhancement","Community preparedness will be strengthened through public education and the enhancement of early warning systems.",""],[1,"106","4","Disaster Insurance Scheme for Vulnerable Groups","Insurance schemes for vulnerable groups and communities will be established and promoted.",""],[1,"106","4","Disaster Response Logistics and Connectivity Enhancement","Also, disaster response capacities, particularly for supply and logistics, will be enhanced to improve surface and air connectivity under the economic development cluster.",""],[1,"115","6","Proactive Disaster Risk Reduction and Preparedness Approach","A proactive approach to disaster risk reduction and preparedness - which also accounts for pandemics and other emergency situations - is an urgent Chapter 6",""]],"44":[[1,"20","1","National Cybersecurity Strategy and Critical Information Infrastructure Protection Framework","Bhutan's digital infrastructure and cybersecurity capabilities will be strengthened with the development of a comprehensive National Cybersecurity Strategy, and the establishment of legal and regulatory frameworks to safeguard critical information infrastructures.",""],[1,"100","2","Cyber Security Strengthening","The 13th FYP shall ensure effective mitigation and management of security threats by enhancing border management and addressing transboundary issues, maintaining internal law and order, and by strengthening cyber security.",""],[1,"108","2","Digital Infrastructure Strengthening and Cybersecurity Initiative","Under the Digital Transformation Programme, led by the GovTech Agency, digital infrastructure will be strengthened while undertaking key initiatives to strengthen cybersecurity.","GovTech Agency"],[1,"108","2","National Cybersecurity Strategy Development","To protect critical information infrastructure and improve cybersecurity culture and society, a comprehensive National Cybersecurity Strategy will be developed and the necessary legal and regulatory frameworks will be put in place.",""],[1,"108","2","Cybersecurity Capacity Building Programme","Cybersecurity capabilities will be built to support the implementation of cybersecurity standards and technologies.",""],[1,"129","2","Cybersecurity and Cyber Resilience Strengthening","Priority attention will be given to implementing robust cybersecurity protocols, fostering a culture of cyber resilience, and safeguarding digital assets.",""]],"45":[[1,"45","4","National Sovereignty and Resilience Safeguarding","Bhutan aims to safeguard its sovereignty and strengthen resilience to any form of threat that could undermine its stability, progress and well-being.",""],[1,"101","1","Critical Infrastructure Protection and Resilience Measures","critical infrastructure will be secured through robust planning, risk management, and investment in infrastructure that is resilient to hazards and disasters.",""],[1,"106","2","Critical Public Infrastructure Disaster Resilience Programme","Critical public infrastructure will be identified, secured and made disaster- resilient.",""]],"46":[[1,"66","3","Digital and Creative Economy Development Initiative","The digital and creative economy will be developed and enhanced as a viable economic sector",""],[1,"66","4","Creative Industry Enabling Infrastructure Investment","Investments in enabling infrastructure for the creative industry will be made to do this.",""],[1,"66","4","National Theatre and Cinema Access Expansion","Theatres and cinemas will be made available throughout Bhutan on various operational modalities.",""],[1,"66","4","Creative Production Studio Development","Several state-of-the-art studios for film and art production will be made available, providing subsidised access to aspiring entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"66","4","Creative Sector Skills Development Support","Investments will be made in supporting skills development and enhancement in the creative sector, such as in editing, script writing, music, direction, photography, dubbing, captioning (SRT), acting and language.",""],[1,"66","4","Intellectual Property Protection and Enforcement","Intellectual Property (IP) protection mechanisms will be strengthened and IP laws will be enforced.",""],[1,"66","5","Digital Infrastructure Strengthening for Nationwide Connectivity","Under the Digital Transformation Programme spearheaded by the GovTech Agency, digital infrastructure will be strengthened to ensure nationwide connectivity with reliable, high-speed and low-cost internet for businesses.","GovTech Agency"],[1,"66","5","Data Centre Expansion for Services Export","Three additional data centres, targeting the export of services will be established.",""],[1,"66","5","Digital Monetisation and Payment Gateway Mechanism","Monetisation options, with payment gateways and digital currency, will be instituted.",""],[1,"128","3","Digitalisation of Industries Initiative","Digitalising Industries: This involves seamless integration of digital technologies across sectors to enhance operational efficiency.",""],[1,"128","4","Digital Business and Innovation Investment","The government will invest in digital businesses and innovation, supporting the establishment of e-commerce platforms, ensuring secure supply chains, facilitating global market access, and embracing emerging technologies.",""],[1,"128","5","GovTech ICT Industry Innovation and Sustainability Initiative","GovTech will foster innovation and sustainability within the ICT sectorto amplify its economic impact.",""],[1,"128","5","ICT Industry Globalisation and Startup Promotion","This will include globalising the industry, nurturing tech startups, and establishing a dedicated IT park.",""],[1,"128","5","Industry-Academia-Government Collaboration for the Data Economy","Additionally, collaboration between industry, academia and government will be strengthened while promoting a data economy and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"129","3","Research and Development Collaboration Strengthening","Strengthening collaboration on research and development among government, industry, and academia will also be a key focus",""],[1,"129","3","Emerging Technology Testbeds","Additionally, the introduction of testbeds will leverage Bhutan's strengths and opportunities, facilitating the exploration of new growth avenues in emerging technologies.",""]],"47":[[1,"144","5","National Spatial Planning for Infrastructure Investment","Infrastructure development will be guided by the national spatial plan to ensure effective investment and growth.",""],[1,"144","5","Efficient Use of Existing Infrastructure and Targeted New Infrastructure Investment","Thus, the 13th FYP will utilise existing infrastructure as appropriate and steer investments toward where there is a clear need to build infrastructure.",""],[1,"144","5","Progressive Strengthening of Spatial Planning for Space Technology","Based on Bhutan's pursuit of space technology, spatial planning will be strengthened progressively.",""]],"48":[[1,"116","4","Boarding Facilities Enhancement","enhancing boarding facilities",""],[1,"144","4","Health and Education Service Standardisation","Health and education services will be realigned to suit Bhutan's needs as it continues to experience persistent migration and its impacts.",""]],"49":[[1,"117","2","National Predictive Data and Analytics System","It will also rely on improved rankings on the GovTech Maturity Index, and the operationalisation of a comprehensive, predictive data and analytics system at the national level.",""],[1,"118","1","Statistical Data Disaggregation and Administrative Data Quality Improvement","This deliverable entails increasing the disaggregation and frequency of published data and statistics beginning 2025, along with strengthening the quality of administrative data across 12 priority sectors: energy, telecom, banking, trade, tourism, tax, traffic, health, education, agriculture, labour and employment, and civil registration.",""],[1,"118","1","Civil Registration and Vital Statistics System Operationalisation","It also involves operationalising a Civil Registration and Vital Statistics (CRVS) system that meets international standards by 2025, and establishing a fully equipped and resourced statistical structure by 2028.",""],[1,"125","1","National Statistics and Statistical Systems Strengthening","To support evidence-based decision-making and service delivery across all sectors, comprehensive national statistics will be developed and statistical systems will be strengthened.",""],[1,"125","1","Statistical Policy and Strategy Reform","The appropriate statistical policies and strategies will be instituted, and an improved data methodology will be adopted.",""],[1,"125","2","Administrative Data and Statistics Strengthening","This will entail ensuring data archival and confidentiality, improving quality of administrative data, rationalising data collection, ensuring availability of high frequency and high-quality data and statistics, and producing disaggregated data at the lowest levels.",""],[1,"125","2","Timebound Interdisciplinary Research Programme","In addition, timebound interdisciplinary research will be conducted.",""],[1,"125","2","Civil Registration and Vital Statistics System","A world-class Civil Registration and Vital Statistics will also be put in place.",""]],"50":[[1,"124","6","Electoral Policy and System Reform","The electoral process and democratic governance will be strengthened, by reviewing and reforming electoral policies and systems as needed.",""],[1,"124","6","Online Voting System Exploration","By leveraging technology, the Election Commission of Bhutan (ECB) will explore online voting systems.",""]],"51":[[1,"60","2","Small Business Finance Access Support Programme","Efforts will be made to improve access to finance, particularly for smaller businesses.",""],[1,"60","2","Financial Incentives, Credit Schemes and Investment Engagement Programmes","This will include the design of financial incentives, credit schemes and investment engagement programmes - complemented by fostering financial literacy.",""],[1,"60","2","Financial Literacy Promotion Initiative","This will include the design of financial incentives, credit schemes and investment engagement programmes - complemented by fostering financial literacy.",""],[1,"60","2","Capital Market Regulatory Reform and Coordination","The overall financial ecosystem will be enhanced through regulatory reforms that promote capital markets and ensure seamless coordination among different actors.",""],[1,"60","3","Company Listing Promotion","The listing of companies will be encouraged to help deepen the capital market, and to provide an alternative investment avenue for the general public.",""],[1,"60","3","Liquidity Injection for Financial Institutions","the government will inject liquidity in financial institutions to enhance private sector access to credit where appropriate, while also encouraging alternative means of lending beyond collateral-based lending.",""],[1,"60","3","Alternative Lending Expansion","the government will inject liquidity in financial institutions to enhance private sector access to credit where appropriate, while also encouraging alternative means of lending beyond collateral-based lending.",""]],"52":[[1,"70","6","Circular Economy Promotion and Enterprise Development","Promotion of a circular economy will be prioritised as part of efforts to ensure sustainable consumption and production practices in Bhutan.",""],[1,"71","1","Waste Material Recovery and Incineration Facilities","facilities for waste material recovery and incinerators, and enhancement of the Integrated Waste Information Management System.",""],[1,"71","1","Integrated Waste Information Management System Enhancement","facilities for waste material recovery and incinerators, and enhancement of the Integrated Waste Information Management System.",""],[1,"71","2","Green Growth Policy and Regulatory Reform","Necessary reforms in policies and regulations will be undertaken to facilitate green growth.",""],[1,"71","2","Online Environmental Clearance Application System","This includes the development of online environmental clearance applications aligned with the Integrated Business Licensing System.",""]],"53":[[1,"18","3","Work-Life Balance and Non-Discriminatory Workplace Reform","Structural and legal reforms will be pursued to promote work-life balance including non-discriminatory workplace policies, flexible working arrangements and addressing barriers to child adoption.",""],[1,"93","3","Work-Life Balance and Family Support Measures","This requires the promotion of work-life balance and associated positive interventions that encourage couples to have children.",""],[1,"93","6","Structural and Legal Reforms for Work-Life Balance","the government will pursue structural and legal reforms to promote work-life balance, empowering individuals and families to enhance their own social security.",""],[1,"94","2","Non-Discriminatory Workplace and Family-Friendly Work Policy Measures","Exploratory measures include the implementation of non-discriminatory workplace policies; fostering shared responsibilities and ensuring conducive conditions for childbearing, flexible and remote working avenues; matching working hours with childcare hours; and addressing barriers to child adoption.",""]],"54":[[1,"19","2","Secure Supply of Critical Energy, Food, and Medical Supplies","5) A secure supply of critical energy, essential food items, and medical food.",""]],"55":[[1,"37","3","13th FYP Support for Gelephu Mindfulness City","the 13th FYP will seamlessly support the vision of the Gelephu Mindfulness City, a unique initiative of His Majesty the King for the future of Bhutan: its children.",""]],"56":[[1,"102","7","Brand Bhutan Promotion and International Engagement","Bhutan's global credibility will be enhanced by promoting Brand Bhutan and maintaining a reputation based on trust, credibility and integrity.",""],[1,"103","1","UN Peacekeeping Participation and International Commitments Delivery","strategic contributions to be made to a global agenda, including through the UN Peacekeeping Programme, and by upholding and delivering on commitments to the climate agenda and the SDGs.",""],[1,"103","2","Consular and Embassy Outreach to Bhutanese Communities Abroad","It requires fostering connections with Bhutanese communities abroad through eligible consular services, construction of chancery offices, events organised by embassies, missions and consulates, and the engagement of eligible youth in the Gyalsung programme.",""],[1,"107","5","Diaspora Engagement Through Embassies and Missions","Bhutan's embassies, missions and consulates will ensure their meaningful engagement in nationally and culturally significant events.",""],[1,"107","5","National Service Programme for Bhutanese Youth Abroad","Eligible Bhutanese youth abroad will also be engaged through the National Service Programme.",""],[1,"107","5","Diaspora Business Linkage and Investment Facilitation","These events will also identify and facilitate opportunities for business linkages and investments in Bhutan.",""],[1,"107","6","International Engagement and Brand Bhutan Promotion","Through effective engagement with the international community and by promoting Brand Bhutan, it will enhance its global credibility.",""],[1,"107","6","Strengthening Bilateral Relations and Peaceful Coexistence","Moreover, the government will continue to maintain friendly and cooperative relations with all countries for peaceful co-existence and promote a just, peaceful and secure international environment.",""]],"57":[[1,"115","5","Integration of Climate Action into Local Plans","Integration of climate action into local plans, especially for key urban centres, and building resilience to the impacts of climate change are critical for Bhutan.",""],[1,"115","5","Climate Resilience Capacity Strengthening","However, this requires strengthened capacities for taking climate action - which encompasses improved climate data and research, integration of climate change into education, and technical capacities for understanding and implementing international environmental legal instruments.",""]],"58":[[1,"127","1","Bhutan Integrated Taxation System Implementation","Accordingly, the Bhutan Integrated Taxation System (BITS) and the Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) will be implemented.",""],[1,"127","1","Integrated Financial Management Information System Implementation","Accordingly, the Bhutan Integrated Taxation System (BITS) and the Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) will be implemented.",""],[1,"127","1","Integration of Existing Digital Finance Systems","Existing systems like ePEMS, eGP, GIMS, ZEST and eDATS will also be integrated and systems like the electronic Customs Management System (eCMS), BRIMS and the property tax system will be enhanced with the support of the GovTech Agency.",""],[1,"127","1","Digital Customs, Revenue, and Property Tax System Enhancement","Existing systems like ePEMS, eGP, GIMS, ZEST and eDATS will also be integrated and systems like the electronic Customs Management System (eCMS), BRIMS and the property tax system will be enhanced with the support of the GovTech Agency.",""]],"59":[[1,"128","6","Digital Inclusion for Civic Participation and Secure Online Use","The 13th FYP will prioritise investments in creating a secure and cohesive society through the strategic use of digital technologies.",""],[1,"128","7","Digital Literacy and Skills Development Programmes","The GovTech Agency will implement digital literacy and skills development programmes by training over 400,000 citizens on the safe use of online services including AI, online banking, video conferencing, and social media platforms, among other components.","GovTech Agency"],[1,"128","8","Digital Platforms for Volunteerism and Charitable Donations","digital platforms will be developed and enhanced to facilitate volunteerism, donations for charitable causes, and other community-building activities towards promoting community vitality.",""],[1,"129","2","Digital Workforce Education and Training Initiative","A skilled digital workforce will be developed through comprehensive education and training initiatives.",""]],"60":[[1,"133","13","Common Minimum Infrastructure Delivery Prioritization","Funds provided through Project Tied Works (SDP and PTA) shall be prirotized to ensure delivery of the CMIs.",""],[1,"135","4","Chiwog Roads Improvement and Local Infrastructure Development","Allocated for Chiwog roads improvement, water supply and irrigation, chain :unselected: link fencing, flood protection, land development and tourism product development among others priortizing the CMIs defined under 7.2.",""],[1,"135","6","Centrally Coordinated Local Government Infrastructure Projects","Centrally coordinated projects for LGs, such as education facilities and :unselected: services, healthcare services, Gewog centre roads, larger irrigation and drinking water schemes, digital infrastructure and services, and human settlement planning and utilities in Dzongkhags.",""],[1,"136","5","Dzongkhag Throm Infrastructure Funding Allocation","each of the 18 Dzongkhags, excluding Thimphu and Samdrupjongkhar, shall allocate 10% of their annual grants and SDP funds to the 18 Dzongkhag Throms.",""],[1,"144","2","Infrastructure Development for Connectivity, Production, and Trade","Meanwhile, it will allow the government to focus on building infrastructure for undisrupted connectivity, production and trade, as well as on removing policy barriers and streamlining public service delivery.",""],[1,"144","3","Economic Transformation Programme","As detailed in the Economic Transformation Programme, the 13th FYP will broaden the infrastructure base to support economic activities, upgrade and maintain connectivity, incentivise use and adoption of technology, and enable skilling for a market- ready workforce.",""]],"61":[[1,"153","1","Economic Stimulus Programme","The Economic Stimulus Programme (ESP) is an urgent measure undertaken by the Government to stimulate the economy to quickly revive the distressed economy.",""],[1,"154","5","ESP Cabinet Oversight and Steering Committee Mechanism","The Cabinet shall be the ultimate authority for making decisions on the implementation of the ESP.",""],[1,"154","6","ESP Secretariat Delivery Unit","The ESP Secretariat, established within the Office of Cabinet Affairs and Strategic Coordination under the Cabinet Secretariat, will serve as a delivery unit for ESP.",""],[1,"154","6","ESP Implementation Coordination and Monitoring","The primary role of the Secretariat will be to coordinate and monitor the implementation of ESP.",""],[1,"154","7","Integration of ESP Projects and Activities into the Annual Budget","The ESP projects and activities shall be incorporated into the annual budget and submitted to the Parliament as part of the annual budget appropriation bill by the Government every year.",""],[1,"154","8","Annual State of the Nation Reporting on ESP Implementation","The nation shall be updated on the progress of the implementation of the ESP through the State of the Nation Report by the Hon'ble Prime Minister on an annual basis.",""]],"62":[[1,"153","4","Education Sector Investment Package","The investments shall be made through a combination of fiscal and monetary measures.",""],[1,"153","4","Ecosystem Investment Support for Value Chain Development","Common investments to create the required ecosystem based on value chain analysis shall be made through fiscal measures",""],[1,"153","4","Affordable Credit Facility for Priority Investments","affordable credit shall be made available through the financial institutes under the supervision of the Royal Monetary Authority.",""],[1,"154","4","Distressed Business Support under Non-Performing Loans","Business reinvigoration: Support to help distressed businesses under Non- Performing Loans.",""]],"63":[[1,"105","17","National Single Window for Trade Facilitation","A national single window for automating trade facilitation will be established.",""]]}});